Don Ciccio...

9
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:20,840
You killed my husband because he wouldn't give in to you.

10
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:23,910
And his oldest son Paolo...

11
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,780
because he swore revenge.

12
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:32,140
But Vito is only nine.And dumb-witted.

13
00:04:32,150 --> 00:04:33,810
He never speaks.

14
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:36,750
It's not his words I'm afraid of.

15
00:04:37,690 --> 00:04:42,880
He's weak. He couldn't hurt anyone.

16
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:45,620
But when he grows, he'll grow strong.

17
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:49,990
Don't worry. This little boy can't do a thing to you.

18
00:04:56,730 --> 00:05:01,370
When he's a man, he'll come for revenge.

19
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:04,260
I beg you, Don Ciccio,spare my only son.

20
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:06,870
He's all I have left.

21
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,230
He's all I have left.

22
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:13,060
I swear to God he'll never do you any harm.

23
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:15,440
Spare him!

24
00:05:20,050 --> 00:05:21,820
No.

25
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:25,470
Run, Vito!

26
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,540
Move and I'll kill him!

27
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:31,540
Run, Vito!

28
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:39,820
Kill him...

29
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:51,120
Any family who hides the boy Vito Andolini will regret it!

30
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:55,290
You understand?

31
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:05,230
Anybody who hides the boy

32
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:11,940
If anyone is hiding the boy Vito Andolini...

33
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:18,270
...turn him over to us.

34
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:22,200
Don Ciccio will thank you for it!

35
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:33,940
Any family who hides the boy Vito Andolini...

36
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:37,580
Vito, we're praying for you!

37
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:46,180
Anybody who hides the boy Vito Andolini is in for trouble!

38
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:48,810
Turn him over to us.

39
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:53,210
Don Ciccio will thank you for it!

40
00:06:53,220 --> 00:07:01,390
It'll be better for the boy,and better for you!

41
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:15,930
Any family who hides the boy Vito Andolini...

42
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,740
Nurse.

43
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,350
Interpreter!

44
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:26,920
Where are you from?

45
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,760
What is your name?

46
00:09:34,270 --> 00:09:38,100
Come on, son. What is your name?

47
00:09:38,110 --> 00:09:40,610
What is your name?

48
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:47,410
Vito Andolini from Corleone.

49
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:51,070
Corleone. Vito Corleone.

50
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:54,640
Okay, over there.

51
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:56,470
Next.

52
00:09:57,050 --> 00:09:58,620
Your name?

53
00:10:05,150 --> 00:10:09,180
Tell him he has smallpox. Quarantine three months.

54
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:24,330
Vito Corleone!Vito Corleone!

55
00:10:25,530 --> 00:10:28,160
Here he is. This is him.

56
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:17,210
Did you bring the car keys?

57
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:22,350
Laurie! Laurie!

58
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:43,460
Mama!

59
00:12:45,230 --> 00:12:46,730
Mama!

60
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:50,360
Look,who's here?

61
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:51,950
- Father Carmelo.-

62
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:54,060
- This is Father Carmelo. - I'm Merle Johnson.

63
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:55,660
family parish.

64
00:12:56,970 --> 00:13:00,630
Mama!Here I am.

65
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,500
Constanzia,

66
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:03,900
after one week?

67
00:13:03,910 --> 00:13:07,870
I sent the car to the airport last week to pick you up.

68
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,170
It was chaos.

69
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:11,540
Anyway, here I am, just one week late.

70
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:14,370
This is for my mama!

71
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:16,410
- What is this? - You remember Merle?

72
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,570
Hello,mama.

73
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:20,010
Hello. How are you? Thank you.

74
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:22,170
Where's Michael? I gotta to talk to him,

75
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,380
and um, get a few things straight,

76
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:25,180
and I can't wait on line.

77
00:13:25,790 --> 00:13:28,340
You go see your children first.

78
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:34,250
Then you worry about waiting on line to see your brother. Like everybody else.

79
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:40,690
Ladies and gentlemen...

80
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,520
A most distinguished guest would like to say a few words.

81
00:13:45,530 --> 00:13:48,090
Please welcome Senator Pat Geary

82
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,800
of the State of Nevada.

83
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:52,290
And there is Mrs. Geary.

84
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,300
Thank you very much, Ladies and Gentlemen

85
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:12,370
This is a very, very happy day for me and my wife Mrs. Geary.

86
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:15,900
We see Nevada far too seldom.

87
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:19,730
But today we can join with old friends,

88
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:20,970
we can make new friends,

89
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:25,400
and we help celebrate a young man's first Communion.

90
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:32,540
And also to thank that boy's family for a magnificent contribution to the State.

91
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:35,480
I have here in my hand a cheque

92
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:38,320
made out to the university,

93
00:14:38,330 --> 00:14:41,150
and it is a magnificent endowment

94
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:48,190
in the name of Anthony Vito Corleone.

95
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:53,100
The cheque is signed by that young man's parents,

96
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:57,720
 whom I think we should recognise.

97
00:14:57,870 --> 00:14:59,150
Mike, Pat, Kay. stand up, please. Let the folks see you!

98
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,360
Folks, I want you to join me

99
00:15:01,370 --> 00:15:07,660
in giving a real Nevada thank you to Mr. and Mrs. Michael Corleone!

100
00:15:12,970 --> 00:15:16,260
We also have, as a special added attraction,

101
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:18,330
the Sierra Boys Choir,

102
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:23,300
who have chosen a certain special song

103
00:15:23,310 --> 00:15:26,370
and a special arrangement to

104
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:28,640
honour their host, Mr. Michael Corleone.

105
00:15:28,810 --> 00:15:30,420
Boys.

106
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:48,610
The plaque.

107
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:51,480
Relax.

108
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:55,250
Okay, fellows, did you get that one?

109
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:59,690
Now, Senator, just you and Mrs. Corleone.

110
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:03,090
Okay that's enough, Senator

111
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:07,320
Give me the cheque.

112
00:16:07,330 --> 00:16:10,500
higher,so we can see it.

113
00:16:20,570 --> 00:16:22,230
My lawyer Tom Hagen.

114
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,590
Senator Geary.

115
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:26,740
He arranged everything through your man Turnbull.

116
00:16:26,850 --> 00:16:28,600
Yes, yes.

117
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:30,300
Sit down.

118
00:16:33,210 --> 00:16:37,670
Well I was under the impression that you and I would talk alone.

119
00:16:37,950 --> 00:16:40,740
I trust these men with my life, Senator.

120
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,910
To ask them to leave would be an insult.

121
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,570
Well,

122
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,970
it's perfectly all right with me,

123
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,310
but I am a blunt man

124
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,940
and I intend to speak very frankly to you.

125
00:16:51,950 --> 00:16:57,520
Maybe more frankly than anyone in my position has ever talked to you before.

126
00:16:57,590 --> 00:17:00,850
The Corleone family has done well in Nevada.

127
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:05,890
You own, or control, two major hotels in Vegas,

128
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,720
and one in Reno.

129
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,790
The licences were grandfathered in,

130
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:15,190
so there was no problem with the Gaming Commission.

131
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:18,960
Now my sources tell me

132
00:17:18,970 --> 00:17:22,290
that you plan to make a move against the Tropigala.

133
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,130
They tell me that, within a week,

134
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,630
you're going to move Klingman out.

135
00:17:28,110 --> 00:17:30,070
Quite an expansion.

136
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:34,400
However, it will leave you with a little technical problem.

137
00:17:36,610 --> 00:17:40,180
The licence will still be in Klingman's name.

138
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,530
Turnbull is a good man.

139
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:45,470
Yeah, well, let's cut out the bullshit.

140
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:48,700
I don't want to spend more time here than I have to.

141
00:17:48,710 --> 00:17:51,010
You can have the licence.

142
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:54,040
The price is 250,000 dollars.

143
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:56,950
Plus five per cent of the gross monthly,

144
00:17:56,960 --> 00:18:02,020
of all four hotels, Mr. Corleone.

145
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:09,180
The price for the licence is less than 20,000 dollars,

146
00:18:09,190 --> 00:18:11,360
-Am I right? -That's right.

147
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:15,120
Why would I pay more than that?

148
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:17,890
Because I intend to squeeze you.

149
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:20,390
I don't like your kind of people.

150
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:25,470
I don't like to see you come out to

151
00:18:25,470 --> 00:18:28,830
this clean country in oily hair,dressed up in those silk suits

152
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:32,570
and try to pass yourselves off as decent Americans.

153
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:34,590
I'll do business with you,

154
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:38,840
but the fact is that I despise your masquerade,

155
00:18:38,850 --> 00:18:41,900
the dishonest way you pose yourself.

156
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:44,580
Yourself, and your whole fucking family.

157
00:18:51,810 --> 00:18:53,240
Senator...

158
00:18:54,620 --> 00:18:57,390
...we're both part of the same hypocrisy.

159
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:03,010
But never think it applies to my family.

160
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:09,760
All right, all right.Some people have to play little games.

161
00:19:09,790 --> 00:19:11,490
You play yours.

162
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,220
Let's say that

163
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:18,520
you'll pay me because it's in your interest.

164
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:21,790
I want your answer and the money by noon tomorrow.

165
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:26,540
One more thing.Don't you contact me again,ever.

166
00:19:26,570 --> 00:19:29,770
From now on you deal with Turnbull.

167
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:32,730
-Open that door, son. -Senator,

168
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
you can have my answer now if you like.

169
00:19:37,610 --> 00:19:39,900
My offer is this:

170
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:42,300
Nothing.

171
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:46,060
Not even the fee for the gaming licence

172
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:50,180
which I would like you to put up personally.

173
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:56,880
Good afternoon, gentlemen.

174
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:02,570
Ladies! I didn't know you were out here.

175
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:04,340
Honey, we have to go. We're 30 minutes late.

176
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:05,400
Really? I'm sorry.

177
00:20:05,410 --> 00:20:08,010
It's been delightful.

178
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:10,150
It was our pleasure.

179
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:11,980
It was wonderful talking to you.

180
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:57,630
Fredo!

181
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:00,740
Fredo, you son-of-a-bitch,

182
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:01,910
you look great!

183
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,770
Frank Pentangeli!

184
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:07,370
I thought you was never coming out west you big bum!

185
00:21:07,950 --> 00:21:10,640
I've got to check on my boys.

186
00:21:10,650 --> 00:21:13,440
What's with the food here?

187
00:21:13,450 --> 00:21:16,280
-What's the matter? -A kid comes up to mein a white jacket,

188
00:21:16,290 --> 00:21:19,840
gives me a Ritz cracker, and uh, chopped liver, he says Canap茅s.

189
00:21:19,850 --> 00:21:25,590
uh, uh, can o' peas my ass, that's a Ritz cracker and chopped liver!

190
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,010
Hey, does anyone...

191
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:30,320
We got a barbecue here, so where's the sausage?

192
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:32,090
Bring out the peppers and sardines!

193
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:35,790
Seeing you reminds me of New York in the old days!

194
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:39,090
Hey, Fredo.You remember Willi Cicci

195
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:44,100
who was with old man Clemenza in Brooklyn?

196
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:46,960
We were all upset about that.

197
00:21:47,170 --> 00:21:48,520
Heart attack, huh?

198
00:21:48,530 --> 00:21:50,220
No, that was no heart attack.

199
00:21:50,230 --> 00:21:53,260
That's what I'm here

200
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:55,540
to see your brother Mike about.

201
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:58,670
- But what's with him? - What do you mean?

202
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:02,170
Do I have to get a letter of introduction

203
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:03,970
to get a sit-down?

204
00:22:04,210 --> 00:22:06,310
You can't get in to see Mike?

205
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:09,080
He's got me waiting in a lobby!

206
00:22:12,250 --> 00:22:13,640
Johnny Ola.

207
00:22:13,650 --> 00:22:15,350
Al Neri.

208
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:20,050
How are you, Johnny?

209
00:22:20,950 --> 00:22:22,740
Do you know my lawyer Tom Hagen?Johnny Ola.

210
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:26,320
Sure,I remember Tom from the old days.

211
00:22:26,330 --> 00:22:29,380
Rocco,what's this?

212
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:31,620
It's an orange from Miami.

213
00:22:32,150 --> 00:22:35,220
Take care of Johnny's men. They look like they might be hungry.

214
00:22:35,230 --> 00:22:36,550
Johnny!

215
00:22:37,700 --> 00:22:39,390
Sit down!

216
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,750
Tom won't stay,Johnny.

217
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,320
He only handles specific areas of the business.

218
00:22:43,330 --> 00:22:44,420
Tom

219
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:46,130
Sure, Mike.

220
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:52,420
What are you drinking, Johnny?

221
00:22:52,570 --> 00:22:54,060
Anisette.

222
00:22:54,870 --> 00:22:56,500
Anisette.

223
00:22:59,110 --> 00:23:01,570
If you need anything,Mike,I'll be outside.

224
00:23:01,580 --> 00:23:03,900
Just tell Rocco we're waiting, Tom.

225
00:23:09,610 --> 00:23:12,240
I just left Mr. Roth in Miami.

226
00:23:12,250 --> 00:23:13,710
How is his health?

227
00:23:13,750 --> 00:23:15,510
It's not good.

228
00:23:16,780 --> 00:23:19,670
Is there anything I can do? Anything I can send?

229
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:24,380
We appreciate your concen Michael and your respect.

230
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:28,750
That casino...Registered owners: Jacob Lawrence,

231
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:31,540
Allan Barclay. Beverly Hills attorneys.

232
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:35,080
The real owners are the old Lakeville Road group

233
00:23:35,090 --> 00:23:39,740
and our friend in Miami.Meyer Klingman runs the store.

234
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:42,050
he runs a piece of it too,he does alright.

235
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:43,550
but I've been instructed to tell you

236
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,350
that if you move him out,

237
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:48,180
our friend in Miami will go along.

238
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:52,260
It's very kind of him.

239
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:55,500
Tell him it's greatly appreciated.

240
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:59,630
Hyman Roth always makes money for his partners.

241
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,830
One by one,

242
00:24:02,840 --> 00:24:04,830
