243
00:24:05,310 --> 00:24:06,960
Death

244
00:24:07,070 --> 00:24:08,830
natural or not,

245
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:12,040
prison, deported...

246
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:15,370
Hyman Roth is the only one left,

247
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:18,670
because he always made money for his partners.

248
00:24:19,970 --> 00:24:21,470
I can't believe it!

249
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:23,400
out of thirty professional musicians,

250
00:24:23,410 --> 00:24:25,870
there isn't one Italian in, in the group here.

251
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:28,710
Let's have a tarantella! Come on!

252
00:24:34,250 --> 00:24:36,920
You! Up! Clarinet up , up, up!

253
00:24:45,850 --> 00:24:47,560
Questa mano!

254
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:50,520
Questa mano!

255
00:24:56,430 --> 00:25:00,790
What the hell have we here?

256
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,330
I'll see my sister alone.

257
00:25:12,670 --> 00:25:16,070
It concerns me too.Is it okay, Mike, if I stay?

258
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:17,630
How are you, honey?

259
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:20,040
You've met Merle, he was with me in Vegas.

260
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:22,140
I saw him with you.

261
00:25:22,340 --> 00:25:24,040
Could I have a drink or something?

262
00:25:26,010 --> 00:25:27,680
Que voi?

263
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:30,700
Al, would you please get him a drink!

264
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:33,870
We're going to Europe next week.

265
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:36,150
I'd like to book passage on the Queen.

266
00:25:36,380 --> 00:25:37,640
So what do you come to me for?

267
00:25:37,650 --> 00:25:39,320
Why don't you go to a travel agent?

268
00:25:39,490 --> 00:25:41,480
We're getting married first.

269
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:52,210
The ink on your divorce isn't dry yet,

270
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:53,890
and you're getting married?

271
00:25:56,660 --> 00:25:59,150
You see your children on weekends.

272
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:02,890
You know your oldest boy, Victor, was picked up in Reno for some petty theft

273
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:04,560
-that you don't even know about. -Mikey.

274
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:06,720
You fly around the world with men who don't even care about you,

275
00:26:06,730 --> 00:26:09,120
-and use you like a whore!-You're not my father!

276
00:26:09,130 --> 00:26:10,560
Then what do you come to me for?

277
00:26:10,570 --> 00:26:12,130
'Cause I need money.

278
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:28,800
Connie, Connie, Connie...

279
00:26:34,610 --> 00:26:36,780
I wanna be reasonable with you.

280
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:41,710
Why don't you stay with the family?

281
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:44,910
You can live on the estate with your kids.

282
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:46,580
You won't be deprived of anything.

283
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:48,580
and you can have everything you want.

284
00:26:53,020 --> 00:26:54,310
I don't know this Merle.

285
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:59,080
I don't know what he does or what he lives on.

286
00:27:00,050 --> 00:27:02,190
Now why don't you tell him marriage is out of the question

287
00:27:02,190 --> 00:27:04,450
and you don't want to see him anymore.

288
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:07,680
He'll understand, believe me.

289
00:27:15,630 --> 00:27:17,330
Connie.

290
00:27:19,610 --> 00:27:21,530
If you don't listen to me,

291
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:23,960
and marry this man...

292
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,130
...you'll disappoint me.

293
00:28:06,660 --> 00:28:08,150
What's "Chen dannay"?

294
00:28:09,090 --> 00:28:12,250
"Cent' anni". It means 100 years.

295
00:28:12,260 --> 00:28:15,050
It means we should all live happily for 100 years.

296
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:16,520
The family.

297
00:28:16,530 --> 00:28:18,520
That'd be true if my father were still alive.

298
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:20,130
Connie!

299
00:28:22,130 --> 00:28:23,260
Merle!

300
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:25,430
you've met my sister-in-law Deanna.

301
00:28:26,270 --> 00:28:27,360
Fredo's wife.

302
00:28:27,370 --> 00:28:29,090
- My pleasure.-How do you do.

303
00:28:29,100 --> 00:28:32,160
-They're perfect. -mama.

304
00:28:32,170 --> 00:28:33,730
What did she mean by that?

305
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:36,830
With all respect,

306
00:28:37,080 --> 00:28:43,240
I didn't come here to eat dinner!

307
00:28:43,250 --> 00:28:45,500
I know, I know.

308
00:29:15,430 --> 00:29:17,850
What's the matter? I just, I just want to dance!

309
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:20,380
Dancing is one thing, you're fallin' all over the floor.

310
00:29:20,390 --> 00:29:21,960
I know what's the matter with you

311
00:29:21,970 --> 00:29:24,320
You're just jealous because he's a real man!

312
00:29:24,330 --> 00:29:26,960
I swear to God, Deanna, I'm gonna belt you right in the teeth.

313
00:29:26,970 --> 00:29:29,260
You couldn't belt your mama!

314
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:31,390
You know somethin'? These Dagos

315
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:32,990
are crazy when it comes to their wives.

316
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:35,800
Michael says that if you can't take care of this,

317
00:29:35,810 --> 00:29:37,570
I have to.

318
00:29:38,370 --> 00:29:39,830
Maybe you better.

319
00:29:39,900 --> 00:29:41,420
Never marry a Wop.

320
00:29:41,430 --> 00:29:43,300
They treat their wives like shit!

321
00:29:43,310 --> 00:29:45,090
I didn't mean to say Wop.

322
00:29:45,570 --> 00:29:49,530
Ahh, Ahh woo! Rocco! Oh!

323
00:29:49,540 --> 00:29:54,070
What are you doing to me, you big slob? Help!Fredo!

324
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,670
I can't control her, Mikey.

325
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:56,870
You're my brother,

326
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:59,000
you don't have to apologize to me.

327
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:04,440
Clemenza promised the Rosato brothers

328
00:30:04,450 --> 00:30:06,840
three territories in the Bronx after he died.

329
00:30:06,850 --> 00:30:08,540
You took over and didn't give it to them.

330
00:30:08,550 --> 00:30:09,710
- I weltched? -You weltched.

331
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:13,050
Clemenza promised them lu cazzo,

332
00:30:13,060 --> 00:30:15,020
Clemenza promised them nothing.

333
00:30:15,030 --> 00:30:17,780
He hated those son of a bitches more than I do.

334
00:30:17,790 --> 00:30:19,910
Frankie, they feel cheated.

335
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:24,150
You're sitting up in the Sierra Mountains

336
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:26,450
and you're drinking...What's he drinking?

337
00:30:26,460 --> 00:30:27,510
Champagne.

338
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:29,480
...Champagne cocktails

339
00:30:29,490 --> 00:30:31,190
and passing judgement on

340
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:32,980
how I run my family.

341
00:30:33,330 --> 00:30:38,090
Your family's still called Corleone.

342
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:41,620
And you'll run it like a Corleone.

343
00:30:41,630 --> 00:30:45,600
My family doesn't eat here, doesn't eat in Las Vegas...

344
00:30:45,610 --> 00:30:47,730
...and doesn't eat in Miami...

345
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:49,670
...with Hyman Roth!

346
00:30:56,070 --> 00:31:00,240
You're a good old man, and I like you.

347
00:31:00,710 --> 00:31:03,570
You were loyal to my father for years.

348
00:31:04,450 --> 00:31:08,830
The Rosato brothers are taking hostages.

349
00:31:09,650 --> 00:31:12,920
They spit right in my face,

350
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:15,810
all because they're backed up by that Jew in Miami.

351
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:17,180
I know.

352
00:31:17,190 --> 00:31:18,780
That's why I don't want them touched.

353
00:31:18,790 --> 00:31:20,450
- Not touched? - No

354
00:31:20,460 --> 00:31:22,110
I want you to be fair with them.

355
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:24,850
You want me to be fair with them?

356
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:29,550
How can you be fair to animals?

357
00:31:29,560 --> 00:31:31,950
Tom, listen. They recruit spics,

358
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,990
they recruit niggers.

359
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:37,990
They do violence in their grandmothers'neighbourhoods!

360
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:44,360
And everything with them is whores! And junk, dope!

361
00:31:44,370 --> 00:31:46,900
And they leave the gambling to last.

362
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:48,860
I want to run my family

363
00:31:48,870 --> 00:31:50,260
without you on my back.

364
00:31:50,270 --> 00:31:53,830
-and I want those Rosato brothers dead! - No.

365
00:31:53,970 --> 00:31:55,570
Mort'

366
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:04,200
Now I have business that's important with Hyman Roth.

367
00:32:04,210 --> 00:32:06,340
I don't want it disturbed.

368
00:32:07,610 --> 00:32:11,000
Then you give your loyalty to a Jew before your own blood.

369
00:32:13,810 --> 00:32:15,130
Come on, Frankie,

370
00:32:15,140 --> 00:32:17,830
You know my father did business with Hyman Roth.

371
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:19,210
He respected him.

372
00:32:19,220 --> 00:32:21,610
Your father did business with Hyman Roth,

373
00:32:21,620 --> 00:32:24,140
he respected Hyman Roth,

374
00:32:24,150 --> 00:32:27,110
but he never trusted Hyman Roth

375
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:30,140
or his Sicilian messenger boy Johnny Ola.

376
00:32:30,150 --> 00:32:37,520
You'll have to excuse me. I'm tired, and I'm a little drunk!

377
00:32:38,390 --> 00:32:40,950
I want everybody here to know,

378
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:43,980
there's not going to be no trouble from me!

379
00:32:43,990 --> 00:32:45,990
Don Corleone.

380
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:48,620
Cicci, the door...

381
00:32:56,370 --> 00:32:58,190
You want him to leave now?

382
00:33:01,040 --> 00:33:02,830
Let him go back to New York.

383
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:04,730
I've already made my plans.

384
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:09,010
The old man had too much wine.

385
00:33:13,540 --> 00:33:15,100
It's late.

386
00:33:27,490 --> 00:33:28,870
How's the baby?

387
00:33:29,580 --> 00:33:31,510
Sleeping inside me.

388
00:33:32,550 --> 00:33:34,010
Does it feel like a boy?

389
00:33:34,020 --> 00:33:37,190
Yes, it does, Michael.

390
00:33:39,490 --> 00:33:40,850
Kay?

391
00:33:41,450 --> 00:33:43,880
I'm sorry about all the people today.

392
00:33:44,090 --> 00:33:48,020
Bad timing.It couldn't be helped, though.

393
00:33:48,330 --> 00:33:51,320
It made me think of what you once told me.

394
00:33:53,670 --> 00:33:57,980
"In five years the Corleone family will be completely legitimate."

395
00:33:57,990 --> 00:34:00,600
That was seven years ago.

396
00:34:03,270 --> 00:34:04,930
I know.

397
00:34:05,470 --> 00:34:08,390
I'm trying, darling.

398
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:02,830
"Do you like it"

399
00:35:10,900 --> 00:35:12,560
Did you see this?

400
00:35:27,470 --> 00:35:29,740
Michael,why are the drapes open?

401
00:35:57,120 --> 00:35:59,110
Kay, are you all right?

402
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:01,080
- Are you hit? - No.

403
00:36:03,860 --> 00:36:05,850
It's over It's over.

404
00:36:08,190 --> 00:36:10,520
Get the door locked!

405
00:36:11,500 --> 00:36:13,890
Stop,stop...

406
00:36:24,200 --> 00:36:25,630
They're still on the property.

407
00:36:25,640 --> 00:36:27,930
Please stay inside.

408
00:36:27,940 --> 00:36:29,060
Keep them alive.

409
00:36:29,070 --> 00:36:32,140
- We'll try.-Alive!

410
00:36:33,110 --> 00:36:34,780
Stay by the door.

411
00:36:38,880 --> 00:36:41,940
Stay around house.

412
00:37:54,810 --> 00:37:56,340
Yeah, come in.

413
00:38:03,650 --> 00:38:05,170
Mike, are you all right?

414
00:38:05,180 --> 00:38:07,180
- Yeah.

415
00:38:10,730 --> 00:38:12,960
Yeah,there's a lot I can't tell you.

416
00:38:15,230 --> 00:38:17,150
and I now that's upset you in the past.

417
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:18,890
A little.

418
00:38:19,730 --> 00:38:23,750
You felt it was because of some lack of trust or confidence.

419
00:38:25,070 --> 00:38:26,590
But it's...

420
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:30,130
because I admire you and love you,

421
00:38:30,140 --> 00:38:32,900
that I kept things secret from you.

422
00:38:34,640 --> 00:38:39,030
Now you're the only one I can trust.

423
00:38:40,510 --> 00:38:42,240
Fredo?

424
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,670
Well, he's got a good heart.

425
00:38:44,900 --> 00:38:47,530
But he's weak and he's stupid

426
00:38:47,540 --> 00:38:50,280
nd this is life and death.

427
00:38:50,450 --> 00:38:54,100
Tom, you're my brother.

428
00:38:59,490 --> 00:39:05,080
I always wanted to be thought of as a brother by you, Mikey. A real brother.

429
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:08,950
I know that.

430
00:39:15,390 --> 00:39:17,420
You're going to take over.

431
00:39:18,420 --> 00:39:20,210
You're going to be the Don.

432
00:39:23,590 --> 00:39:26,520
If what I think has happened,

433
00:39:26,930 --> 00:39:29,090
I'm leaving here tonight.

434
00:39:29,960 --> 00:39:31,920
I give you complete power.

435
00:39:31,930 --> 00:39:36,360
Over Fredo and his men. Rocco, Neri, everyone.

436
00:39:37,740 --> 00:39:41,270
I'm trusting you with the lives of my wife

437
00:39:41,300 --> 00:39:43,120
and my children,

438
00:39:43,170 --> 00:39:45,090
the future of this family.

439
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,430
If we catch them,

440
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:51,660
will we find out...

441
00:39:51,670 --> 00:39:53,640
We won't catch them.

442
00:39:54,670 --> 00:39:55,960
Unless I'm very wrong,

443
00:39:55,970 --> 00:39:58,010
they're dead already.

444
00:39:59,720 --> 00:40:02,370
They were killed by somebody close to us.

445
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:04,740
Inside.

446
00:40:04,750 --> 00:40:08,240
Very,very frightened that they botched it.

447
00:40:08,250 --> 00:40:10,640
You don't think that Rocco and Neri

448
00:40:10,650 --> 00:40:12,820
had something to do with this?

449
00:40:15,990 --> 00:40:17,510
See...

450
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:20,760
All our people are businessmen.

451
00:40:21,850 --> 00:40:24,750
Their loyalty is based on that.

452
00:40:27,250 --> 00:40:29,960
One thing I learned from Pop...

453
00:40:31,270 --> 00:40:35,720
...was to try to think as people around you think.

454
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:39,760
On that basis, anything is possible.

455
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:45,520
Mike, they're dead! Right outside my window!

456
00:40:45,530 --> 00:40:48,890
I want to get out of here.They're lying there dead!

457
00:40:48,900 --> 00:40:50,220
Get her in!

458
00:40:59,940 --> 00:41:02,900
Over here! There's two of them.

459
00:41:02,910 --> 00:41:04,640
Looks like they were hired out of New York.

460
00:41:04,650 --> 00:41:06,610
I don't recognise them.

461
00:41:07,580 --> 00:41:09,070
Won't get anything out of them now.

462
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:10,460
Look,look...

463
00:41:10,470 --> 00:41:12,370
Fish them out.

464
00:41:37,200 --> 00:41:39,260
Get rid of the bodies.

465
00:41:39,490 --> 00:41:40,820
Where's Mike?

466
00:41:40,830 --> 00:41:42,390
Rocco.

467
00:42:12,580 --> 00:42:18,540
Anthony, everything is going to be all right. Try to sleep.

468
00:42:34,050 --> 00:42:36,290
Did you like your party?

469
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:40,450
- I got lots of presents.-I know.

470
00:42:40,990 --> 00:42:42,480
Did you like them?

471
00:42:42,530 --> 00:42:46,060
Yeah. I didn't know the people who gave them to me.

472
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:48,760
Well, they were friends.

473
00:42:50,670 --> 00:42:53,020
Did you see my present for you?

474
00:42:53,030 --> 00:42:54,800
It was on my pillow.

475
00:42:57,530 --> 00:42:58,720
Anthony.

476
00:42:58,730 --> 00:43:01,260
I'm going to be leaving very early tomorrow.

477
00:43:01,270 --> 00:43:06,030
- Will you take me? - No, I can't, Anthony.

478
00:43:06,040 --> 00:43:08,160
Why do you have to go?

479
00:43:09,010 --> 00:43:11,100
I have to do business.

480
00:43:11,740 --> 00:43:13,740
I could help you.

481
00:43:18,350 --> 00:43:20,700
I know. Some day you will.

482
00:43:21,580 --> 00:43:23,350
Get some sleep.

483
00:44:40,580 --> 00:44:43,780
She's really beautiful.You've got to see her.

484
00:45:03,830 --> 00:45:08,900
Wait till you see her. Words can't describe her.

485
00:45:17,500 --> 00:45:22,660
I left Naples. I left Mama.

486
00:45:22,670 --> 00:45:26,300
For a no-good tramp!

487
00:45:26,310 --> 00:45:32,100
Now here I am in America, in New York.

488
00:45:32,780 --> 00:45:37,540
Alone! Thinking of my mother.

489
00:45:38,610 --> 00:45:41,380
Without news from home.

490
00:45:43,050 --> 00:45:44,510
Enter!

491
00:45:44,550 --> 00:45:47,410
Pepino, a letter for you!

492
00:45:47,820 --> 00:45:49,320
Have a seat.

493
00:45:49,520 --> 00:45:52,810
Finally, a letter from Naples!

494
00:45:54,420 --> 00:45:57,990
Vito, how do you like my little angel?

495
00:45:58,350 --> 00:46:00,650
Isn't she beautiful?

496
00:46:00,660 --> 00:46:02,150
She's very beautiful.

497
00:46:02,160 --> 00:46:03,510
To you, she's beautiful.

498
00:46:03,520 --> 00:46:06,290
For me, there's only my wife and son.

499
00:46:06,490 --> 00:46:08,820
And mama

500
00:46:10,390 --> 00:46:19,530
Our dear mother is dead!

501
00:47:07,490 --> 00:47:12,880
We'll go backstage later and take her to eat.

502
00:47:16,700 --> 00:47:21,870
Sit down, you bum!

503
00:47:25,160 --> 00:47:28,690
Oh, excuse me, Don Fanucci.

504
00:47:35,440 --> 00:47:38,530
We'll go see her backstage.

505
00:47:40,700 --> 00:47:45,280
-Who was that?-The Black Hand.

506
00:47:58,120 --> 00:48:01,780
Vito,come on...

507
00:48:01,790 --> 00:48:03,950
Come on let's go see her backstage.

508
00:48:05,150 --> 00:48:08,050
Sorry,sorry...

509
00:48:12,750 --> 00:48:17,150
Please.

510
00:48:17,220 --> 00:48:19,080
That's Fanucci... the Black Hand.

511
00:48:19,090 --> 00:48:22,480
We'll talk about it tomorrow.

512
00:48:23,030 --> 00:48:30,620
Tomorrow! Always tomorrow!

513
00:48:30,930 --> 00:48:37,830
You'll pay me today!

514
00:48:39,460 --> 00:48:40,830
Let's go.

515
00:48:41,400 --> 00:48:48,700
-Pay me now! -Not my daughter! Let her go!

516
00:48:48,710 --> 00:48:53,560
Here, take all my money!

517
00:48:58,280 --> 00:49:01,020
Vito, come on.

518
00:49:03,880 --> 00:49:08,880
I know what you're thinking.

519
00:49:08,890 --> 00:49:10,880
But you don't know how things are.

520
00:49:10,890 --> 00:49:12,610
Fanucci's with the Black Hand.

521
00:49:12,620 --> 00:49:15,050
The whole neighborhood pays him.

522
00:49:15,060 --> 00:49:17,140
Even my father, in the grocery store.

523
00:49:17,150 --> 00:49:18,380
If he's Italian...

524
00:49:18,390 --> 00:49:20,640
...why does he bother other Italians?

525
00:49:20,650 --> 00:49:22,920
He knows they have nobody to protect them.

526
00:49:22,930 --> 00:49:27,780
Forget that. Did you like my angel?

527
00:49:27,790 --> 00:49:29,930
If you're happy, I'm happy.

528
00:50:17,820 --> 00:50:19,380
Don't you feel well?

529
00:50:23,920 --> 00:50:26,350
Is your boss treating you all right?

530
00:50:27,420 --> 00:50:29,240
Forget it.

531
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:33,790
Hey! Paisan!

532
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:45,020
Hey, you speak Italian?

533
00:50:51,100 --> 00:50:56,060
Hide this for me!Next week. I'll come and get it!

534
00:51:34,760 --> 00:51:40,390
Abbandando, meet my nephew!

535
00:51:41,860 --> 00:51:44,990
How's business?

536
00:51:49,830 --> 00:51:53,150
It's good, it's good.

537
00:51:57,730 --> 00:52:02,800
Fanucci's mad. Says the neighborhood's getting sloppy.

538
00:52:02,810 --> 00:52:07,470
People don't pay on time, don't pay the full amount.

539
00:52:07,480 --> 00:52:10,170
Says he's been too nice to everyone.

540
00:52:15,210 --> 00:52:17,570
So Fanucci's changing?

541
00:52:17,580 --> 00:52:20,800
Sure. He wants double from everybody.

542
00:52:20,810 --> 00:52:25,280
Even from my father.

543
00:52:25,820 --> 00:52:27,680
I'm a friend, right?

544
00:52:27,690 --> 00:52:32,380
So you'll let him work here?

545
00:52:45,390 --> 00:52:48,990
Vito,come here.

546
00:52:57,630 --> 00:53:02,090
I've got some bad news.

547
00:53:04,210 --> 00:53:10,930
I feel rotten about telling you this...

548
00:53:10,940 --> 00:53:17,290
But Fanucci... he's got a nephew...And you have to give him my job.

549
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:25,270
You've always been good to me, ever since I came here.

550
00:53:25,280 --> 00:53:30,080
You looked after me like a father.

551
00:53:30,090 --> 00:53:38,380
I thank you.And I won't forget it.

552
00:53:50,920 --> 00:53:52,310
Vito!

553
00:53:57,190 --> 00:53:58,960
No...

554
00:53:59,500 --> 00:54:00,820
Oh, no!

555
00:54:00,830 --> 00:54:04,890
Take this to your family.

556
00:54:04,900 --> 00:54:07,050
Thanks anyway. But please, I can't accept.

557
00:54:07,060 --> 00:54:11,420
-Take this to your family. -I can't accept.

558
00:54:11,430 --> 00:54:13,140
No!

559
00:54:42,310 --> 00:54:44,780
What a nice pear!

560
00:55:07,530 --> 00:55:11,060
I'm Clemenza, you still have my goods?

561
00:55:13,240 --> 00:55:15,970
Did you look inside?

562
00:55:16,970 --> 00:55:20,500
I'm not interested in things that don't concern me.

563
00:55:30,980 --> 00:55:33,670
A friend of mine has a nice rug.

564
00:55:33,680 --> 00:55:36,170
Maybe your wife would like it.

565
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:45,810
Sure she would. But who has money for a rug?

566
00:55:45,820 --> 00:55:53,040
It would be a present. I know how to return a favor.

567
00:55:59,620 --> 00:56:04,410
Yeah,sure.My wife would like it.

568
00:56:07,630 --> 00:56:09,680
Let's go

569
00:56:27,900 --> 00:56:33,300
The son of a bitch! He isn't home!

570
00:56:34,140 --> 00:56:37,470
Damn, he didn't even leave the key.

571
00:56:41,170 --> 00:56:43,670
Well, he won't mind.

572
00:56:54,480 --> 00:56:59,210
Come on in. Hey,Vito come on in.

573
00:56:59,220 --> 00:57:02,150
Please come on in.

574
00:57:22,330 --> 00:57:26,360
-This is your friend's place? -Yes.

575
00:57:26,800 --> 00:57:29,060
This is a real palace.

576
00:57:29,170 --> 00:57:31,200
One of the best.

577
00:57:37,500 --> 00:57:40,230
Vito, give me a hand, will you?

578
00:59:36,390 --> 00:59:39,560
Look how pretty it is, Santino!

579
01:02:08,590 --> 01:02:10,200
Come on in.

580
01:02:12,430 --> 01:02:15,950
It's all right. Hyman's in there.

581
01:02:15,960 --> 01:02:18,450
Would you like a tuna sandwich?

582
01:02:18,460 --> 01:02:20,100
No, thank you.

583
01:02:31,510 --> 01:02:33,000
Mr. Roth?

584
01:02:33,580 --> 01:02:35,140
Come in, Michael.

585
01:02:36,940 --> 01:02:39,870
Sit down, make yourself comfortable.

586
01:02:41,440 --> 01:02:43,610
It's almost over.

587
01:02:45,520 --> 01:02:47,440
Do you follow the football game?

588
01:02:48,920 --> 01:02:50,870
Not for a while I haven't.

589
01:02:50,890 --> 01:02:53,910
I enjoy watching football in the afternoon.

590
01:02:53,920 --> 01:02:56,590
One of the things I love about this country.

591
01:02:56,790 --> 01:02:58,790
Baseball too.

592
01:02:59,030 --> 01:03:03,780
Ever since Arnold Rothstein fixed the World Series in 1919.

593
01:03:10,930 --> 01:03:13,160
I heard you had some trouble.

594
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:18,060
Stupid.

595
01:03:19,060 --> 01:03:22,130
People behaving like that with guns.

596
01:03:23,970 --> 01:03:26,200
The important thing is you're all right.

597
01:03:26,870 --> 01:03:30,860
Good health is the most important thing.

598
01:03:30,870 --> 01:03:34,030
More than success, more than money.

599
01:03:35,410 --> 01:03:37,340
More than power.

600
01:03:51,550 --> 01:03:54,640
I came here because there's going to be more bloodshed.

601
01:03:55,520 --> 01:03:57,640
I wanted you to know

602
01:03:57,650 --> 01:04:00,250
so another war won't start.

603
01:04:00,550 --> 01:04:02,610
Nobody wants another war.

604
01:04:03,620 --> 01:04:06,110
Frank Pentangeli asked my permission

605
01:04:06,120 --> 01:04:09,550
to get rid of the Rosato brothers.

606
01:04:09,560 --> 01:04:11,970
When I refused he tried to have me killed.

607
01:04:11,980 --> 01:04:13,610
He was stupid, I was lucky.

608
01:04:13,620 --> 01:04:15,320
I'll visit him soon.

609
01:04:15,500 --> 01:04:20,750
The important thing is that nothing interferes with ourplans for the future.

610
01:04:20,760 --> 01:04:23,620
Nothing is more important.

611
01:04:25,900 --> 01:04:28,950
You're a wise and considerate man.

612
01:04:28,960 --> 01:04:31,200
And you're a great man, Mr. Roth.

613
01:04:31,930 --> 01:04:33,860
There's much I can learn from you.

614
01:04:34,570 --> 01:04:37,060
Whatever I can do to help, Michael.

615
01:04:39,070 --> 01:04:41,970
- Excuse me. Lunch. - Come in.

616
01:04:42,140 --> 01:04:43,790
Thank you, my dear.

617
01:04:43,800 --> 01:04:46,970
You're going to break your eardrums.

618
01:04:47,710 --> 01:04:50,230
- Enjoy it. - Thank you.

619
01:04:55,920 --> 01:04:58,640
You're young, I'm old and sick.

620
01:04:59,890 --> 01:05:04,880
What we'll do in the next few months will make history.

621
01:05:04,890 --> 01:05:07,750
It's never been done before.

622
01:05:07,760 --> 01:05:12,640
Not even your father would dream that such a thing could be possible.

623
01:05:14,320 --> 01:05:19,140
Frank Pentangeli is a dead man. You don't object?

624
01:05:20,430 --> 01:05:22,580
He's small potatoes.

625
01:05:33,230 --> 01:05:34,790
What's up?

626
01:05:37,970 --> 01:05:40,060
We got company?

627
01:05:54,330 --> 01:05:59,920
-Michael Corleone is here. -Michael Corleone?

628
01:05:59,930 --> 01:06:04,730
He's in your den. You better hurry.

629
01:06:04,740 --> 01:06:07,060
He's been waiting a half hour.

630
01:06:13,680 --> 01:06:16,070
Is something wrong?

631
01:06:19,930 --> 01:06:21,390
Don Corleone

632
01:06:21,400 --> 01:06:22,990
I wish you would have let me know you were coming.

633
01:06:23,000 --> 01:06:25,520
I could have prepared something.

634
01:06:25,530 --> 01:06:28,130
I didn't want you to know.

635
01:06:34,870 --> 01:06:36,560
You heard what happened?

636
01:06:36,570 --> 01:06:38,160
I almost died.

637
01:06:38,170 --> 01:06:41,030
-We were so relieved.-In my home!

638
01:06:43,870 --> 01:06:47,300
In my bedroom where my wife sleeps!

639
01:06:49,610 --> 01:06:52,570
Where my children come to play.

640
01:06:53,710 --> 01:06:55,710
In my home.

641
01:07:12,790 --> 01:07:15,740
I want you to help me take my revenge.

642
01:07:15,750 --> 01:07:20,790
Michael, anything. What can I do?

643
01:07:22,730 --> 01:07:25,650
Settle these troubles with the Rosato brothers.

644
01:07:26,060 --> 01:07:27,820
I don't understand. I don't...

645
01:07:27,830 --> 01:07:30,690
I don't have your brain

646
01:07:30,700 --> 01:07:32,060
for big deals.

647
01:07:32,070 --> 01:07:33,660
But this is a street thing.

648
01:07:33,670 --> 01:07:38,860
That Hyman Roth in Miami. He's backing up those sons-of-bitches.

649
01:07:38,870 --> 01:07:40,030
I know he is.

650
01:07:40,040 --> 01:07:41,390
Then why?

651
01:07:41,400 --> 01:07:44,510
So why ask me to lay down to them?

652
01:07:49,450 --> 01:07:52,410
It was Hyman Roth that tried to have me killed.

653
01:07:54,620 --> 01:07:56,380
I know it was him.

654
01:07:57,820 --> 01:07:59,940
Jesus Christ, Mike.

655
01:08:00,250 --> 01:08:03,680
Jesus Christ, let's get them all.

656
01:08:03,690 --> 01:08:05,510
Now while we've got the muscle.

657
01:08:10,420 --> 01:08:13,490
This used to be my father's old study.

658
01:08:14,300 --> 01:08:16,060
It's changed.

659
01:08:17,630 --> 01:08:19,300
I remember...

660
01:08:20,160 --> 01:08:22,160
there used to be a big desk here.

661
01:08:25,030 --> 01:08:29,900
I remember when I was a kid. We had to be quiet when we played near here.

662
01:08:37,600 --> 01:08:41,630
I was very happy that this house never went to strangers.

663
01:08:42,710 --> 01:08:46,970
First Clemenza took it over. Now you.

664
01:08:48,380 --> 01:08:51,080
My father taught me many things here.

665
01:08:51,180 --> 01:08:53,080
He taught me in this room.

666
01:08:56,880 --> 01:09:00,570
He taught me, "Keep your friends close,

667
01:09:00,580 --> 01:09:02,920
but your enemies closer."

668
01:09:03,050 --> 01:09:06,550
If Hyman Roth sees that I interceded in this

669
01:09:06,560 --> 01:09:08,950
in the Rosato brothers' favour

670
01:09:09,330 --> 01:09:12,320
he'll think his relationship with me is still good.

671
01:09:12,330 --> 01:09:15,560
-Capide? -Capide.

672
01:09:15,700 --> 01:09:17,860
That's what I want him to think.

673
01:09:18,830 --> 01:09:20,860
I want him relaxed

674
01:09:20,870 --> 01:09:23,660
and confident in our friendship.

675
01:09:23,670 --> 01:09:25,130
Then I'll be able to find out

676
01:09:25,140 --> 01:09:28,060
who the traitor in my family was.

677
01:09:56,580 --> 01:09:58,950
Fredo, this is Johnny Ola

678
01:09:59,160 --> 01:10:02,010
We need some more help,Johnny

679
01:10:02,020 --> 01:10:03,620
Johnny?

680
01:10:04,120 --> 01:10:06,890
Jesus Christ, what the hell time is it?

681
01:10:07,300 --> 01:10:08,680
Who's that, honey?

682
01:10:08,830 --> 01:10:10,320
Listen good, Fredo,

683
01:10:10,330 --> 01:10:12,120
Why are you calling me?

684
01:10:12,130 --> 01:10:13,720
I don't want to talk to you.

685
01:10:13,730 --> 01:10:18,290
Pentangeli is going to accept the Rosato brothers' deal

686
01:10:18,330 --> 01:10:20,920
- Will he come alone?-I don't know.

687
01:10:20,930 --> 01:10:22,630
You've got me in deep enough already.

688
01:10:22,640 --> 01:10:23,990
Just go along,

689
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:25,440
everything will be all right,

690
01:10:25,440 --> 01:10:28,330
 Fredo,Pentangeli says he's willing to make a deal

691
01:10:28,340 --> 01:10:32,730
All we want to know is if he's on the level, or if he'll bring his boys

692
01:10:32,740 --> 01:10:35,900
You lied to me. I don't want you to call me anymore.

693
01:10:35,910 --> 01:10:38,230
Your brother won't find out we talked

694
01:10:38,240 --> 01:10:40,270
I don't know what you're talking about.

695
01:10:51,350 --> 01:10:52,910
Who was that?

696
01:10:53,050 --> 01:10:55,450
Wrong number.

697
01:11:03,760 --> 01:11:05,410
Frankie, I've got nobody here.

698
01:11:05,420 --> 01:11:06,650
Wait in the car, Cicc'.

699
01:11:06,660 --> 01:11:09,230
- Frankie. - That's okay, Cicc'.

700
01:11:16,460 --> 01:11:17,860
What's this?

701
01:11:17,870 --> 01:11:20,190
A lucky C note for our new deal.

702
01:11:23,270 --> 01:11:26,100
Ritchie. Give us a taste.

703
01:11:30,240 --> 01:11:33,770
We were all real happy about your decision, Frankie.

704
01:11:34,240 --> 01:11:36,000
You won't regret it.

705
01:11:36,010 --> 01:11:38,640
I don't like the C note, Rosato.

706
01:11:38,650 --> 01:11:41,080
I take that as an insult.

707
01:11:41,440 --> 01:11:44,370
Michael Corleone says hello!

708
01:12:01,000 --> 01:12:04,160
Close the door!

709
01:12:04,160 --> 01:12:05,650
Your friend the cop...

710
01:12:06,500 --> 01:12:09,170
Hey, Ritch. It's dark in here.

711
01:12:09,200 --> 01:12:10,790
Are you open or closed?

712
01:12:10,800 --> 01:12:13,900
I just came in to clean up a little, you know?

713
01:12:17,010 --> 01:12:18,730
What's the matter?

714
01:12:19,370 --> 01:12:20,890
Is that something on the floor?

715
01:12:20,900 --> 01:12:24,860
Carmine, not here! Anthony!

716
01:12:26,970 --> 01:12:29,830
You open this bar and I'll blow your head in!

717
01:13:16,470 --> 01:13:18,630
Freddy, it's good to see you.

718
01:13:21,410 --> 01:13:26,600
- How is he? - He's okay. He's in the back.

719
01:13:29,810 --> 01:13:32,200
Girls, take a hike.

720
01:13:35,580 --> 01:13:37,580
In this room here.

721
01:13:40,220 --> 01:13:42,070
I want to talk to him alone first.

722
01:13:42,080 --> 01:13:43,580
Come on.

723
01:13:52,530 --> 01:13:54,950
I thought I could help you, Senator.

724
01:13:59,160 --> 01:14:00,730
Hagen?

725
01:14:02,320 --> 01:14:04,560
Listen, I did not...

726
01:14:04,570 --> 01:14:06,590
It's all right.

727
01:14:06,600 --> 01:14:07,920
I didn't do anything.

728
01:14:07,930 --> 01:14:09,490
It's okay.

729
01:14:10,070 --> 01:14:11,960
You're very lucky.

730
01:14:12,270 --> 01:14:14,890
My brother Fredo operates this place.

731
01:14:14,900 --> 01:14:17,070
He was called before anyone.

732
01:14:17,870 --> 01:14:19,230
Had this happened some place else

733
01:14:19,240 --> 01:14:20,970
we couldn't have helped you.

734
01:14:24,670 --> 01:14:27,410
When I woke up, I was on the floor.

735
01:14:29,310 --> 01:14:31,370
And I don't know how it happened.

736
01:14:31,380 --> 01:14:33,170
You can't remember?

737
01:14:37,110 --> 01:14:39,110
I passed out.

738
01:14:55,460 --> 01:14:57,310
Just a game. Jesus.

739
01:14:57,320 --> 01:15:02,360
Jesus, Jesus!

740
01:15:08,800 --> 01:15:12,130
Jesus God!

741
01:15:15,670 --> 01:15:17,130
Oh God!

742
01:15:22,410 --> 01:15:25,370
I don't know, and I don't understand why

743
01:15:25,380 --> 01:15:26,540
I can't remember.

744
01:15:26,550 --> 01:15:29,440
Doesn't matter, just do as I say.

745
01:15:29,450 --> 01:15:31,910
Put in a call to your office.

746
01:15:31,920 --> 01:15:33,240
Explain that

747
01:15:33,250 --> 01:15:35,880
you'll be there tomorrow.

748
01:15:36,020 --> 01:15:42,780
You decided to spend the night at Michael Corleone's house in Tahoe.

749
01:15:42,790 --> 01:15:46,210
I do remember that she was laughing.

750
01:15:47,650 --> 01:15:49,390
We'd done it before

751
01:15:49,660 --> 01:15:53,790
and I know that I could not have hurt that girl.

752
01:15:54,160 --> 01:15:56,020
This girl has no family.

753
01:15:56,030 --> 01:15:58,720
Nobody knows that she worked here.

754
01:15:58,730 --> 01:16:01,260
It'll be as though she never existed.

755
01:16:03,570 --> 01:16:05,860
All that's left is our friendship.

756
01:16:21,250 --> 01:16:22,430
Yes?

757
01:16:22,440 --> 01:16:25,440
Sorry, but we're not to let you through.

758
01:16:26,010 --> 01:16:27,740
I'm just going to the market.

759
01:16:27,750 --> 01:16:30,300
We'll pick up anything you want.

760
01:16:30,310 --> 01:16:31,740
Whose orders are these?

761
01:16:31,750 --> 01:16:33,640
Mr. Hagen's. He's coming.

762
01:16:33,650 --> 01:16:36,620
I'll speak to him.

763
01:16:41,890 --> 01:16:45,750
I wanted to explain, but I had business in Carson City.

764
01:16:45,760 --> 01:16:47,950
It's Michael's request for your safety.

765
01:16:47,960 --> 01:16:50,050
We'll get anything you need.

766
01:16:50,060 --> 01:16:52,690
So I'm supposed to stay in my house?

767
01:16:52,700 --> 01:16:55,130
No, within the compound will be fine.

768
01:16:55,160 --> 01:16:57,620
We were going to New England.

769
01:16:57,630 --> 01:16:59,150
That's off.

770
01:16:59,160 --> 01:17:01,090
Am I a prisoner?

771
01:17:01,100 --> 01:17:02,590
That's not how we see it, Kay.

772
01:17:02,600 --> 01:17:05,560
Come on, kids. We're going back to the house.

773
01:17:07,910 --> 01:17:09,360
Joe.

774
01:17:55,570 --> 01:17:58,330
Cuba, Cuba!

775
01:18:38,230 --> 01:18:40,110
Most respected gentlemen.

776
01:18:41,430 --> 01:18:43,850
Welcome to Havana.

777
01:18:45,690 --> 01:18:50,930
I want to thank this distinguished group of

778
01:18:52,740 --> 01:18:55,120
American industrialists for continuing to work with Cuba

779
01:18:56,440 --> 01:18:58,860
for the greatest period of prosperity

780
01:19:00,530 --> 01:19:02,200
in her entire history.

781
01:19:03,530 --> 01:19:05,000
Mr. William Shaw

782
01:19:05,880 --> 01:19:07,900
representing the General Fruit Company.

783
01:19:09,610 --> 01:19:11,640
Messrs Corngold and Dant

784
01:19:12,410 --> 01:19:14,740
of United Telephone and Telegraph Company.

785
01:19:16,580 --> 01:19:18,140
Mr. Petty

786
01:19:18,180 --> 01:19:22,100
regional Vice President of the Pan American Mining Corporation.

787
01:19:24,060 --> 01:19:26,880
Mr. Robert Allen of South American Sugar.

788
01:19:28,450 --> 01:19:31,380
Mr. Michael Corleone of Nevada.

789
01:19:32,620 --> 01:19:36,650
representing our associates in tourism and leisure activities.

790
01:19:37,290 --> 01:19:40,690
And my old friend and associate from Florida.

791
01:19:42,360 --> 01:19:44,360
Mr. Hyman Roth.

792
01:19:44,630 --> 01:19:46,590
I would like to thank

793
01:19:46,600 --> 01:19:48,990
United Telephone and Telegraph

794
01:19:49,000 --> 01:19:50,390
for their Christmas gift.

795
01:19:55,170 --> 01:19:57,440
A solid gold telephone.

796
01:19:59,940 --> 01:20:01,900
Perhaps you gentlemen would like to look at it.

797
01:20:04,170 --> 01:20:05,970
- Mr. President? - Yes?

798
01:20:05,980 --> 01:20:09,860
Could you discuss the rebel activity

799
01:20:09,870 --> 01:20:12,200
and what this can mean to our businesses?

800
01:20:12,210 --> 01:20:13,600
- Of course. - Heavy stuff.

801
01:20:13,610 --> 01:20:15,070
I assure you that

802
01:20:15,120 --> 01:20:16,970
lthough the rebels have started

803
01:20:16,980 --> 01:20:19,720
a campaign in Las Villas

804
01:20:25,650 --> 01:20:28,210
my staff indicates, with assurance

805
01:20:28,220 --> 01:20:33,080
that we'll drive them out of Santa Clara before the New Year.

806
01:20:35,690 --> 01:20:37,660
I want to put you all at ease.

807
01:20:38,360 --> 01:20:42,650
We will tolerate no guerrillas in the casinos or the swimming pools.

808
01:21:01,240 --> 01:21:03,200
He said that they're making an arrest

809
01:21:03,210 --> 01:21:06,040
and in a few minutes he'll let us through.

810
01:21:06,480 --> 01:21:08,740
-Johnny.-It's nothing.

811
01:21:08,750 --> 01:21:12,710
Just some lousy bandits.The police are cleaning them up.

812
01:21:26,550 --> 01:21:28,110
Viva Fidel!

813
01:21:31,990 --> 01:21:34,080
I hope my age is correct.

814
01:21:34,100 --> 01:21:36,880
I'm always accurate about my age.

815
01:21:38,000 --> 01:21:41,690
Make sure that everybody sees the cake before we cut it.

816
01:21:44,830 --> 01:21:46,790
I'm very pleased

817
01:21:47,500 --> 01:21:52,460
you're all able to come from such distances to be with me today.

818
01:21:53,700 --> 01:21:56,970
When a man comes to this point in his life

819
01:21:57,980 --> 01:22:01,570
he wants to turn over the things he's been blessed with.

820
01:22:01,610 --> 01:22:03,560
Turn them over to friends

821
01:22:03,570 --> 01:22:07,180
as a reward for the friends he's had.

822
01:22:07,780 --> 01:22:11,410
and to make sure that

823
01:22:11,420 --> 01:22:13,200
everything goes well after he's gone.

824
01:22:13,210 --> 01:22:14,710
Not for years.

825
01:22:16,090 --> 01:22:18,640
We'll see. The doctors would disagree

826
01:22:18,650 --> 01:22:20,380
but what do they know?

827
01:22:21,460 --> 01:22:26,680
These are wonderful things that we've achieved in Havana

828
01:22:26,690 --> 01:22:29,650
and there's no limit to where we can go from here.

829
01:22:29,660 --> 01:22:34,420
This kind of government knows how to help business,to encourage it.

830
01:22:34,430 --> 01:22:38,650
The hotels here are bigger and swankier than

831
01:22:38,660 --> 01:22:41,660
any of the joints in Vegas.

832
01:22:41,670 --> 01:22:44,760
We can thank our friends in the Cuban government

833
01:22:44,770 --> 01:22:49,530
which has put up half the cash with the Teamsters,on a dollar for dollar basis

834
01:22:49,540 --> 01:22:52,460
and has relaxed restrictions on imports.

835
01:22:52,470 --> 01:22:53,600
What I'm saying is

836
01:22:53,610 --> 01:22:56,830
that we have now what we have always needed:

837
01:22:56,840 --> 01:22:59,740
Real partnership with a government.

838
01:22:59,870 --> 01:23:01,440
Smaller piece.

839
01:23:02,570 --> 01:23:05,300
You all know Michael Corleone

840
01:23:05,310 --> 01:23:07,500
and we all remember his father.

841
01:23:07,510 --> 01:23:11,340
At the time of my retirement, or death

842
01:23:11,350 --> 01:23:15,810
I turn over all my interests in the Havana operation

843
01:23:15,820 --> 01:23:17,340
to his control.

844
01:23:17,350 --> 01:23:19,250
But

845
01:23:19,390 --> 01:23:21,850
all of you will share.

846
01:23:21,860 --> 01:23:25,320
The Nacionale will go to the Lakeville Road Boys

847
01:23:25,330 --> 01:23:28,650
the Capri to the Corleone family

848
01:23:28,660 --> 01:23:31,150
the Sevilla Biltmore also

849
01:23:31,160 --> 01:23:34,820
but Eddie Levine will bring in the Pennino brothers

850
01:23:34,830 --> 01:23:37,760
Dino and Eddie, for a piece

851
01:23:37,770 --> 01:23:39,990
and to handle the casino operations.

852
01:23:40,000 --> 01:23:43,720
We've saved a piece for some friends in Nevada

853
01:23:43,730 --> 01:23:46,970
to make sure that things go smoothly back home.

854
01:23:49,470 --> 01:23:52,470
I want all of you to enjoy your cake.

855
01:23:52,480 --> 01:23:54,670
So, enjoy!

856
01:23:54,680 --> 01:23:55,970
Happy birthday!

857
01:23:58,480 --> 01:24:01,070
I saw an interesting thing happen today.

858
01:24:02,210 --> 01:24:05,540
A rebel was being arrested by the military police.

859
01:24:05,550 --> 01:24:10,170
Rather than be taken alive, he exploded a grenade he had in his jacket.

860
01:24:10,180 --> 01:24:13,610
He killed himself and took a captain of the command with him.

861
01:24:13,620 --> 01:24:16,550
-Right,Johnny?-Those rebels are lunatics.

862
01:24:16,790 --> 01:24:22,740
Maybe so.But it occurred to me,that the soldiers are paidto fight

863
01:24:22,750 --> 01:24:24,290
the rebels aren't.

864
01:24:24,300 --> 01:24:26,120
What does that tell you?

865
01:24:26,660 --> 01:24:28,390
They can win.

866
01:24:30,360 --> 01:24:33,220
This country has had rebels for 50 years.

867
01:24:33,230 --> 01:24:35,080
It's in their blood.I know.

868
01:24:35,090 --> 01:24:37,670
I've been coming here since the Twenties.

869
01:24:37,970 --> 01:24:39,720
We were running molasses from Havana

870
01:24:39,730 --> 01:24:41,550
when you were a baby.

871
01:24:41,870 --> 01:24:44,800
The trucks were owned by your father.

872
01:24:45,510 --> 01:24:47,170
Mikey.

873
01:24:54,210 --> 01:24:57,270
I'd rather we talked about this when we're alone.

874
01:24:59,980 --> 01:25:02,880
The two million never got to the island.

875
01:25:08,790 --> 01:25:12,340
It mustn't be known that you held back the money

876
01:25:12,350 --> 01:25:15,020
because you worried about the rebels.

877
01:25:21,160 --> 01:25:25,450
Sit down, Michael. Sit down.

878
01:25:32,370 --> 01:25:36,820
If I could only live to see it, to be there with you.

879
01:25:38,570 --> 01:25:43,700
What I wouldn't give for 20 more years.

880
01:25:44,540 --> 01:25:47,130
Here we are, protected.

881
01:25:47,140 --> 01:25:49,500
Free to make our profits without Kefauver

882
01:25:49,510 --> 01:25:53,230
the goddamn Justice Department and the FBI .

883
01:25:53,240 --> 01:25:54,870
90 miles away

884
01:25:54,880 --> 01:25:57,470
in partnership with a friendly government.

885
01:25:58,120 --> 01:26:02,210
90 miles. It's nothing.

886
01:26:02,520 --> 01:26:05,650
Just one small step for a man looking to

887
01:26:05,660 --> 01:26:08,410
be President of the United States

888
01:26:08,420 --> 01:26:11,520
and having the cash to make it possible.

889
01:26:11,860 --> 01:26:13,310
Mikey!

890
01:26:15,060 --> 01:26:17,220
we're bigger than U.S. Steel.

891
01:26:44,410 --> 01:26:47,370
Mikey, how are you? Okay?

892
01:26:48,680 --> 01:26:51,500
Hi! Freddie Corleone.

893
01:26:51,770 --> 01:26:53,480
Mio frati

894
01:26:54,780 --> 01:26:57,070
Jesus Christ, what a trip!

895
01:26:57,080 --> 01:26:58,240
I thought, "What if somebody knows

896
01:26:58,250 --> 01:27:00,450
what I've got in here".

897
01:27:00,610 --> 01:27:01,840
Can you imagine that?

898
01:27:01,850 --> 01:27:05,450
Two million dollars on the seat next to me.

899
01:27:09,280 --> 01:27:11,890
- Excuse me. - It's okay.

900
01:27:13,390 --> 01:27:15,060
You want to count it?

901
01:27:19,890 --> 01:27:21,990
What's going on?

902
01:27:22,260 --> 01:27:23,490
I'm totally in the dark.

903
01:27:23,500 --> 01:27:25,660
The family is making an investment in Havana.

904
01:27:25,670 --> 01:27:27,870
This is a gift for the President.

905
01:27:29,070 --> 01:27:32,860
That's great! Havana's great.

906
01:27:34,240 --> 01:27:36,270
It's my kind of town.

907
01:27:37,570 --> 01:27:39,570
Anybody I know in Havana?

908
01:27:39,680 --> 01:27:42,770
Don't know. Hyman Roth, Johnny Ola?

909
01:27:45,350 --> 01:27:48,910
No. I've never met them.

910
01:27:51,650 --> 01:27:54,080
Listen, Mikey, I'm kind of...

911
01:27:54,220 --> 01:27:55,910
...kind of

912
01:27:59,550 --> 01:28:01,240
nervous from the trip.

913
01:28:01,250 --> 01:28:04,650
Can I get a drink or something?

914
01:28:04,720 --> 01:28:07,490
I thought maybe we'd go out together.

915
01:28:07,950 --> 01:28:11,620
I know a place where we can spend some time together.

916
01:28:13,560 --> 01:28:16,620
Sometimes I think I should have married a woman like you did.

917
01:28:16,760 --> 01:28:23,430
Like Kay.Have kids. Have a family.

918
01:28:24,310 --> 01:28:26,460
For once in my life

919
01:28:26,770 --> 01:28:30,900
be more like Pop..

920
01:28:32,970 --> 01:28:35,570
It's not easy to be a son, Fredo.

921
01:28:36,100 --> 01:28:37,730
It's not easy.

922
01:28:37,740 --> 01:28:41,100
Mama used to say, "You don't belong to me."

923
01:28:41,110 --> 01:28:47,270
"You were left on the doorstep by gypsies."Sometimes I think it's true.

924
01:28:47,750 --> 01:28:49,980
You're no gypsy, Fredo.

925
01:28:51,220 --> 01:28:52,940
Mikey... I...

926
01:28:53,190 --> 01:28:55,480
I was mad at you.

927
01:29:02,830 --> 01:29:05,780
Why didn't we spend time like this before?

928
01:29:06,560 --> 01:29:08,410
You want a drink, right?

929
01:29:08,420 --> 01:29:10,190
Waiter!

930
01:29:16,660 --> 01:29:18,360
How do you say Banana Daquiri?

931
01:29:18,370 --> 01:29:19,780
Banana Daquiri.

932
01:29:19,790 --> 01:29:22,030
- That's it? - That's it.

933
01:29:22,170 --> 01:29:24,060
Uno Banana Daquiri.

934
01:29:24,070 --> 01:29:25,520
Banana Daquiri.

935
01:29:26,400 --> 01:29:28,100
and a club soda.

936
01:29:35,570 --> 01:29:38,200
Senator Geary flies in from Washington tomorrow

937
01:29:38,210 --> 01:29:40,670
with some government people.

938
01:29:40,680 --> 01:29:43,610
I want you to show them a good time in Havana.

939
01:29:46,280 --> 01:29:48,520
That's my speciality, right?

940
01:29:48,810 --> 01:29:51,100
Can I trust you with something?

941
01:29:51,110 --> 01:29:52,680
Of course, Mike.

942
01:29:55,620 --> 01:30:01,780
Later in the evening we're all invited to the President to bring in the New Year

943
01:30:01,790 --> 01:30:07,640
After it's over they'll take me home in a military car

944
01:30:07,650 --> 01:30:09,590
alone.For my protection.

945
01:30:10,290 --> 01:30:14,220
Before I reach my hotel, I'll be assassinated.

946
01:30:32,010 --> 01:30:35,270
- Who? - Roth.

947
01:30:40,780 --> 01:30:43,740
It was Roth who tried to kill me in my home.

948
01:30:45,520 --> 01:30:47,750
It was Roth all along.

949
01:30:47,980 --> 01:30:50,010
He acts like I'm his son

950
01:30:50,020 --> 01:30:52,080
his successor.

951
01:30:52,950 --> 01:30:54,740
But he thinks he'll live forever

952
01:30:54,750 --> 01:30:56,680
and wants me out.

953
01:31:01,030 --> 01:31:02,550
How can I help?

954
01:31:02,560 --> 01:31:07,620
Just go along, as if you know nothing.I've already made my move.

955
01:31:07,630 --> 01:31:09,260
What move?

956
01:31:09,730 --> 01:31:12,320
Hyman Roth won't see the New Year.

957
01:31:29,610 --> 01:31:32,400
Says you have to take it easy.And he's gonna give you a prescription.

958
01:31:32,410 --> 01:31:34,770
-He'll be back tomorrow. -I want my own doctor.

959
01:31:34,780 --> 01:31:36,200
Fly in my own doctor from Miami.

960
01:31:36,210 --> 01:31:38,600
I don't trust a doctor who can't speak English.

961
01:31:40,010 --> 01:31:43,220
- Gracias, senor - Buenas noches

962
01:31:44,780 --> 01:31:46,800
Honey, go to the casino.

963
01:31:46,810 --> 01:31:48,500
If you're feeling better.

964
01:31:48,510 --> 01:31:50,180
Feel fine.

965
01:31:52,060 --> 01:31:53,820
Play the bingo game.

966
01:31:53,860 --> 01:31:57,380
- Okay. Nice to see you, Mr. Paul.-

967
01:31:58,730 --> 01:32:00,720
My sixth sense tells me Fredo

968
01:32:00,730 --> 01:32:02,720
brought a bag full of money.

969
01:32:02,900 --> 01:32:04,250
Where is it?

970
01:32:06,330 --> 01:32:07,990
You're pulling out?

971
01:32:08,730 --> 01:32:10,400
Just want to...

972
01:32:11,430 --> 01:32:13,200
Just want to wait.

973
01:32:16,300 --> 01:32:20,090
- How do you feel? - Terrible.

974
01:32:20,100 --> 01:32:21,230
I'd give four million to be able

975
01:32:21,240 --> 01:32:24,170
to take a painless piss.

976
01:32:24,300 --> 01:32:26,830
Who had Frank Pentangeli killed?

977
01:32:27,710 --> 01:32:29,940
The Rosato brothers.

978
01:32:30,240 --> 01:32:33,740
I know, but who gave the go-ahead?

979
01:32:34,250 --> 01:32:36,140
I know I didn't.

980
01:32:43,920 --> 01:32:46,940
There was this kid I grew up with.

981
01:32:46,950 --> 01:32:48,620
He was younger than me.

982
01:32:48,920 --> 01:32:51,090
Sort of looked up to me

983
01:32:51,530 --> 01:32:53,220
you know

984
01:32:53,230 --> 01:32:55,550
We did our first work together.

985
01:32:55,590 --> 01:32:57,480
Worked our way out of the street.

986
01:32:57,490 --> 01:33:00,490
Things were good.

987
01:33:00,590 --> 01:33:06,720
During Prohibition we ran molasses into Canada.Made a fortune.

988
01:33:06,730 --> 01:33:08,400
Your father too.

989
01:33:10,270 --> 01:33:14,960
As much as anyone, I loved him and

990
01:33:14,970 --> 01:33:16,760
trusted him.

991
01:33:18,880 --> 01:33:22,570
Later on he had an idea

992
01:33:22,610 --> 01:33:25,900
to build a city

993
01:33:25,910 --> 01:33:29,660
out of a desert stop-over for G.I.s going to the West Coast.

994
01:33:30,580 --> 01:33:33,900
That kid's name was Moe Greene

995
01:33:34,310 --> 01:33:38,480
and the city he invented was Las Vegas.

996
01:33:39,420 --> 01:33:41,450
This was a great man.

997
01:33:42,090 --> 01:33:44,580
A man of vision and guts.

998
01:33:44,590 --> 01:33:48,180
And there isn't even a plaque, signpost

999
01:33:48,190 --> 01:33:51,940
or statue of him in that town.

1000
01:33:52,760 --> 01:33:57,750
Someone put a bullet through his eye.

1001
01:33:57,760 --> 01:34:01,060
No one knows who gave the order.

1002
01:34:01,070 --> 01:34:04,360
When I heard it, I wasn't angry.

1003
01:34:04,370 --> 01:34:06,560
I knew Moe, I knew he was headstrong.

1004
01:34:06,570 --> 01:34:09,830
Talking loud, saying stupid things.

1005
01:34:10,300 --> 01:34:12,730
So when he turned up dead

1006
01:34:13,640 --> 01:34:16,030
I let it go.

1007
01:34:17,040 --> 01:34:19,530
And I said to myself

1008
01:34:20,240 --> 01:34:24,400
This is the business we've chosen.

1009
01:34:24,410 --> 01:34:26,300
I didn't ask

1010
01:34:27,280 --> 01:34:29,240
who gave the order

1011
01:34:29,250 --> 01:34:33,100
because it had nothing to do with business.

1012
01:34:40,890 --> 01:34:46,020
That two million in a bag in your room

1013
01:34:47,650 --> 01:34:51,450
I'm going in to take a nap.

1014
01:34:51,820 --> 01:34:53,490
When I wake

1015
01:34:54,190 --> 01:34:55,680
if the money is on the table

1016
01:34:55,690 --> 01:34:57,630
I know I have a partner.

1017
01:34:57,830 --> 01:35:01,360
If it isn't, I know I don't.

1018
01:35:55,900 --> 01:35:58,290
Does everybody know everybody?

1019
01:35:58,760 --> 01:36:00,390
This is senator Geary,you know him.

1020
01:36:00,400 --> 01:36:02,330
-How are you,senator? -Good to see you, Mike.

1021
01:36:02,340 --> 01:36:04,130
I'm glad we spend this time together.

1022
01:36:04,140 --> 01:36:06,290
Senator Payton from Florida

1023
01:36:06,300 --> 01:36:07,420
How ya doin', Mike?

1024
01:36:07,430 --> 01:36:09,090
Judge DeMalco from New York

1025
01:36:09,100 --> 01:36:10,960
-How do you do, Sir?-Fine, thank you.

1026
01:36:10,970 --> 01:36:12,170
Senator Ream from Maryland

1027
01:36:12,180 --> 01:36:13,870
Mike, I've been looking forward to it.

1028
01:36:13,880 --> 01:36:15,460
Fred Corngold from UTT.

1029
01:36:15,470 --> 01:36:16,560
I know Fred, how are you?

1030
01:36:16,570 --> 01:36:19,100
That Freddie does a mean Cha Cha Cha so watch out later.

1031
01:36:19,110 --> 01:36:20,170
Oh he does, huh?

1032
01:36:20,180 --> 01:36:22,700
Okay,gentlemen,it's refill time here.

1033
01:36:22,710 --> 01:36:24,970
You might try some of those local drinks,

1034
01:36:24,980 --> 01:36:26,170
you know "Cuba Libra"

1035
01:36:26,180 --> 01:36:27,540
"Pi?a Colada"

1036
01:36:27,550 --> 01:36:31,270
I think I'll try one of those red headed Yolandas.

1037
01:36:31,280 --> 01:36:33,640
That you got! Con gusto..

1038
01:36:33,650 --> 01:36:35,220
Johnny!

1039
01:36:35,250 --> 01:36:37,270
You don't know my brother Fredo.

1040
01:36:37,280 --> 01:36:39,140
Johnny Ola, Fredo.

1041
01:36:39,150 --> 01:36:42,420
We never met. Johnny Ola. Pleasure.

1042
01:36:43,860 --> 01:36:46,450
Gentlemen, to a night in Havana!

1043
01:36:46,460 --> 01:36:48,350
- Happy New Year! - Happy New Year!

1044
01:36:48,360 --> 01:36:52,190
- Feliz Ano Nuevo! - Happy New Year.

1045
01:37:02,970 --> 01:37:05,240
Hey, Freddie, why are we standing?

1046
01:37:05,370 --> 01:37:06,860
Everybody stands.

1047
01:37:06,870 --> 01:37:10,090
It's worth it. You won't believe this.

1048
01:37:10,100 --> 01:37:11,740
I don't believe it already.

1049
01:37:11,800 --> 01:37:13,000
50 dollars, right?

1050
01:37:13,010 --> 01:37:14,790
You've got a bet, mister.

1051
01:37:23,110 --> 01:37:24,850
That's Superman.

1052
01:37:58,900 --> 01:38:01,220
Did I tell you or did I tell you?

1053
01:38:02,540 --> 01:38:04,120
I don't believe it!

1054
01:38:04,130 --> 01:38:05,330
It's got to be fake.

1055
01:38:05,340 --> 01:38:08,500
It's real. That's why he's called Superman.

1056
01:38:09,300 --> 01:38:11,460
Hey, Freddy

1057
01:38:11,470 --> 01:38:13,300
where did you find this place?

1058
01:38:13,310 --> 01:38:15,100
Johnny Ola brought me here.

1059
01:38:15,110 --> 01:38:16,460
I didn't believe it

1060
01:38:16,470 --> 01:38:18,400
but seeing is believing!

1061
01:38:18,410 --> 01:38:20,000
I see it, but still don't believe it!

1062
01:38:20,010 --> 01:38:21,270
50 bucks, Pat.

1063
01:38:21,280 --> 01:38:22,800
Roth won't go here

1064
01:38:22,810 --> 01:38:25,810
but Johnny knows these places like the back of his hand.!

1065
01:38:25,950 --> 01:38:28,000
Now watch him,he's gonna break a cracked with it.

1066
01:38:28,010 --> 01:38:31,190
Break a cracker? I want to see him break a brick.

1067
01:38:32,350 --> 01:38:34,350
He could knock down a building.

1068
01:39:52,930 --> 01:39:54,260
Relax!Se?or Roth.

1069
01:39:54,270 --> 01:39:56,270
we're taking you to the hospital.

1070
01:40:45,360 --> 01:40:47,790
And in my judgment, you'll continue to get those,

1071
01:40:47,800 --> 01:40:49,120
because I don't believe

1072
01:40:49,130 --> 01:40:52,230
that President Eisenhower well ever pull out of Cuba

1073
01:40:52,240 --> 01:40:54,560
not as long as we have over one billion dollars

1074
01:40:54,570 --> 01:40:56,430
invested in this country.

1075
01:40:59,340 --> 01:41:02,730
The American public believe in non-intervention...

1076
01:41:02,740 --> 01:41:04,130
Fredo!

1077
01:41:04,410 --> 01:41:05,730
Where are you going?

1078
01:41:05,780 --> 01:41:07,240
I'm getting a real drink

1079
01:41:07,250 --> 01:41:08,980
because I can't...

1080
01:42:05,210 --> 01:42:06,570
What kept Mr. Roth?

1081
01:42:06,580 --> 01:42:08,250
I understood he was coming.

1082
01:42:08,610 --> 01:42:10,840
Reeves, what's the protocol?

1083
01:42:10,850 --> 01:42:12,340
How long should we stay?

1084
01:42:13,650 --> 01:42:15,470
I think a half hour ought to do it.

1085
01:42:15,480 --> 01:42:18,150
Just long enough to bring in the New Year.

1086
01:42:32,430 --> 01:42:40,060
It's New Year's Eve. Come on, just for a minute.

1087
01:43:52,140 --> 01:43:53,740
There's a plane waiting

1088
01:43:53,750 --> 01:43:56,530
to take us to Miami in an hour.

1089
01:43:56,540 --> 01:43:58,510
Don't make a big thing about it.

1090
01:44:02,570 --> 01:44:04,880
I know it was you, Fredo.

1091
01:44:05,010 --> 01:44:06,830
You broke my heart.

1092
01:44:08,010 --> 01:44:10,250
You broke my heart!

1093
01:44:49,810 --> 01:44:55,400
Due to serious setbacks to our troops in Guantanamo and Santiago

1094
01:44:55,410 --> 01:44:59,540
my position in Cuba is untenable.

1095
01:44:59,680 --> 01:45:09,340
I am resigning from office to avoid further bloodshed.

1096
01:45:09,350 --> 01:45:18,150
And I shall leave the city immediately.

1097
01:45:18,160 --> 01:45:27,590
I wish all of you good luck.

1098
01:45:52,310 --> 01:45:56,840
Fredo!Come on. Come with me.

1099
01:45:56,850 --> 01:45:59,170
It's the only way out of here tonight.

1100
01:45:59,180 --> 01:46:01,710
Roth is dead!Fredo.

1101
01:46:01,850 --> 01:46:03,610
Fredo, come with me!

1102
01:46:03,620 --> 01:46:09,150
You're still my brother.Fredo...

1103
01:46:27,230 --> 01:46:28,860
Passports,Passports,U.S. passports only, please.

1104
01:46:32,530 --> 01:46:35,670
Pass through, I'm Pat GEARY of the United States Senate!

1105
01:46:38,840 --> 01:46:41,760
-Get back! -Please, I must leave!

1106
01:47:49,510 --> 01:47:53,150
Al. Get me a wet towel.

1107
01:47:59,520 --> 01:48:01,290
Does Kay know I'm back?

1108
01:48:06,320 --> 01:48:09,650
My boy? Did you get him something for Christmas?

1109
01:48:09,660 --> 01:48:11,320
I took care of it.

1110
01:48:11,330 --> 01:48:12,890
What was it, so I'll know.

1111
01:48:13,130 --> 01:48:16,690
It was a little car with an electric motor that he can ride in.

1112
01:48:16,700 --> 01:48:18,390
It's nice.

1113
01:48:20,940 --> 01:48:22,720
Thank you, Al.

1114
01:48:23,800 --> 01:48:26,560
Fellows, could you step outside for a minute?

1115
01:48:44,350 --> 01:48:46,010
Where's my brother?

1116
01:48:47,110 --> 01:48:49,510
Roth got out on a private boat.

1117
01:48:49,520 --> 01:48:50,670
He's in a hospital in Miami.

1118
01:48:50,680 --> 01:48:53,000
He had a stroke, but recovered okay.

1119
01:48:53,410 --> 01:48:55,270
Your bodyguard is dead.

1120
01:48:55,280 --> 01:48:57,020
I asked about Fredo.

1121
01:48:58,020 --> 01:49:01,190
I think he got out. He must be somewhere in New York.

1122
01:49:04,420 --> 01:49:06,020
All right.

1123
01:49:07,090 --> 01:49:09,250
I want you to get in touch with him.

1124
01:49:10,060 --> 01:49:11,750
I know he's scared.

1125
01:49:11,760 --> 01:49:13,020
Tell him everything is all right.

1126
01:49:13,030 --> 01:49:15,380
Tell him I know Roth misled him.

1127
01:49:15,390 --> 01:49:17,990
That he didn't know they would try to kill me.

1128
01:49:19,560 --> 01:49:21,300
They can come in now.

1129
01:49:21,900 --> 01:49:23,820
There was something else.

1130
01:49:24,570 --> 01:49:25,960
What?

1131
01:49:32,870 --> 01:49:35,200
What? Come on.

1132
01:49:36,600 --> 01:49:39,710
Kay had a miscarriage.

1133
01:49:51,880 --> 01:49:53,150
Was it a boy?

1134
01:49:53,160 --> 01:49:54,510
At three and a half months.

1135
01:49:54,520 --> 01:49:57,480
Can't you give me a straight answer?!

1136
01:49:57,490 --> 01:49:59,380
Was it a boy?

1137
01:50:01,520 --> 01:50:03,450
I really don't know.

1138
01:50:14,260 --> 01:50:22,730
Poor little Fredo, he's got pneumonia.

1139
01:51:06,360 --> 01:51:11,780
Young man, I hear you and your friends are stealing goods.

1140
01:51:11,790 --> 01:51:14,490
But you don't even send a dress to my house.

1141
01:51:14,500 --> 01:51:16,120
No respect!

1142
01:51:16,130 --> 01:51:18,550
You know I've got three daughters.

1143
01:51:18,700 --> 01:51:21,660
This is my neighborhood.

1144
01:51:21,670 --> 01:51:25,530
You and your friends should show me some respect.

1145
01:51:25,540 --> 01:51:29,390
You should let me wet my beak a little.

1146
01:51:31,570 --> 01:51:35,930
I hear you and your friends

1147
01:51:36,010 --> 01:51:39,140
cleared $600 each.

1148
01:51:39,150 --> 01:51:43,970
Give me $200 each, for your own protection.

1149
01:51:43,980 --> 01:51:47,690
And I'll forget the insult.

1150
01:51:48,310 --> 01:51:51,180
You young punks have to learn

1151
01:51:51,190 --> 01:51:54,620
to respect a man like me!

1152
01:51:55,030 --> 01:51:58,250
Otherwise the cops will come to your house.

1153
01:51:58,260 --> 01:52:01,080
And your family will be ruined.

1154
01:52:01,320 --> 01:52:04,050
Of course if I'm wrong about how much you stole

1155
01:52:04,060 --> 01:52:07,350
I'll take a little less.And by less,I only mean a hundred bucks less.

1156
01:52:08,870 --> 01:52:11,360
Now don't refuse me.

1157
01:52:14,630 --> 01:52:18,990
-Understand, paesano? -I understand.

1158
01:52:20,870 --> 01:52:23,900
My friends and I share all the money.

1159
01:52:23,910 --> 01:52:26,370
So first, I have to talk to them.

1160
01:52:26,380 --> 01:52:28,840
Tell your friends

1161
01:52:28,850 --> 01:52:32,770
I don't want a lot. Just enough to wet my beak.

1162
01:52:35,710 --> 01:52:38,110
Don't be afraid to tell them!

1163
01:52:40,550 --> 01:52:42,950
600 bucks.

1164
01:52:43,890 --> 01:52:45,910
Suppose we don't pay?

1165
01:52:45,920 --> 01:52:48,310
You know his gang, Tessio.

1166
01:52:48,320 --> 01:52:49,970
Real animals.

1167
01:52:49,980 --> 01:52:53,250
Maranzalla himself let Fanucci work this neighborhood.

1168
01:52:53,260 --> 01:52:55,750
He's got connections with the cops, too.

1169
01:52:55,760 --> 01:52:57,450
We have to pay him.

1170
01:52:57,460 --> 01:53:01,660
$200 each...everybody agreed?

1171
01:53:05,530 --> 01:53:07,150
Why do we have to pay him?

1172
01:53:07,160 --> 01:53:10,430
Vito, leave this to us.

1173
01:53:10,960 --> 01:53:13,760
He's one person, we're three.

1174
01:53:13,770 --> 01:53:17,060
He's got guns, we've got guns.

1175
01:53:17,070 --> 01:53:20,290
Why should we give him the money we sweated for?

1176
01:53:20,300 --> 01:53:24,200
This is his neighborhood!

1177
01:53:24,470 --> 01:53:30,110
I know two bookies who don't give anything to Fanucci.

1178
01:53:30,680 --> 01:53:38,270
They don't pay Fanucci.

1179
01:53:38,280 --> 01:53:40,940
If they don't pay Fanucci

1180
01:53:40,950 --> 01:53:43,970
then somebody else collects for Maranzalla!

1181
01:53:43,980 --> 01:53:48,410
We'll all be better off if we pay him.

1182
01:53:48,420 --> 01:53:50,060
Don't worry.

1183
01:54:01,730 --> 01:54:07,320
Now what I say stays in this room.

1184
01:54:07,330 --> 01:54:09,330
If you both like

1185
01:54:09,340 --> 01:54:13,800
why not give me $50 each to pay Fanucci?

1186
01:54:15,470 --> 01:54:19,760
I guarantee he'll accept what I give him.

1187
01:54:21,940 --> 01:54:23,830
If Fanucci says $200

1188
01:54:23,840 --> 01:54:25,830
he means it, Vito!

1189
01:54:25,840 --> 01:54:28,000
I'll reason with him.

1190
01:54:28,310 --> 01:54:33,440
Leave everything to me.

1191
01:54:33,450 --> 01:54:35,470
I'll take care of everything.

1192
01:54:35,480 --> 01:54:40,550
I never lie to my friends.

1193
01:54:40,560 --> 01:54:44,340
Tomorrow you both go talk to Fanucci.

1194
01:54:44,350 --> 01:54:46,640
He'll ask for the money.

1195
01:54:46,650 --> 01:54:51,450
Tell him you'll pay whatever he wants.

1196
01:54:51,460 --> 01:54:53,250
Don't argue with him.

1197
01:54:53,260 --> 01:54:55,050
Then I'll go and get him to agree.

1198
01:54:55,060 --> 01:55:02,150
Don't argue with him, since he's so tough.

1199
01:55:02,160 --> 01:55:04,890
How can you get him to take less?

1200
01:55:04,900 --> 01:55:07,190
That's my business.

1201
01:55:07,500 --> 01:55:11,630
Just remember that I did you a favor.

1202
01:55:15,340 --> 01:55:19,540
-Is it a deal? -Si.

1203
01:55:25,880 --> 01:55:27,180
Salute.

1204
01:55:27,190 --> 01:55:29,410
Salute.

1205
01:56:06,800 --> 01:56:09,430
His family's out of the house.

1206
01:56:09,440 --> 01:56:11,760
Fanucci's alone in the cafe.

1207
01:56:16,640 --> 01:56:21,200
Vito, here's my 50 dollars.

1208
01:56:30,220 --> 01:56:34,740
Buona fortuna,are you sure he's going to go for it?

1209
01:56:35,480 --> 01:56:40,480
I'll make an offer he don't refuse.

1210
01:56:40,490 --> 01:56:42,260
Don't worry.

1211
01:57:14,750 --> 01:57:21,280
It looks like there's - $100 under my hat.

1212
01:57:31,620 --> 01:57:37,940
I was right.Only $100...

1213
01:57:39,990 --> 01:57:43,920
I'm short of money right now.

1214
01:57:43,930 --> 01:57:49,420
I've been out of work,so just give me a little time.

1215
01:57:49,430 --> 01:57:52,790
You understand, don't you?

1216
01:58:00,360 --> 01:58:04,500
You've got balls, young man!

1217
01:58:04,970 --> 01:58:08,560
How come I never heard of you before?

1218
01:58:14,450 --> 01:58:18,330
You've got a lot of guts.

1219
01:58:20,920 --> 01:58:24,510
I'll find you some work for good money.

1220
01:58:34,990 --> 01:58:40,020
No hard feelings, right?

1221
01:58:42,130 --> 01:58:45,620
If I can help you, let me know.

1222
01:58:48,130 --> 01:58:50,720
Enjoy the festa!

1223
01:59:07,910 --> 01:59:09,730
Don FANUCCI.

1224
02:00:52,700 --> 02:00:54,520
Forzzelando!

1225
02:01:02,870 --> 02:01:05,040
Oh, this is too violent for me!

1226
02:03:24,800 --> 02:03:27,050
What've you got there?

1227
02:06:03,690 --> 02:06:13,980
Michael, your father loves you very much.

1228
02:09:34,320 --> 02:09:37,650
Mr. Cicci, from the year 1942 to the present time,

1229
02:09:37,950 --> 02:09:40,940
you were an employee of the Genco Olive Oil Company?

1230
02:09:41,410 --> 02:09:43,080
That's right.

1231
02:09:43,940 --> 02:09:45,130
But in actuality

1232
02:09:45,140 --> 02:09:48,630
you were a member of the Corleone crime organisation.

1233
02:09:51,010 --> 02:09:53,790
No, we called it the Corleone family,

1234
02:09:53,800 --> 02:09:55,390
Senator.we called it the family.

1235
02:09:55,400 --> 02:09:57,320
What was your position?

1236
02:09:58,630 --> 02:10:01,910
At first, like everybody else, I was a soldier.

1237
02:10:01,920 --> 02:10:03,050
What is that?

1238
02:10:03,060 --> 02:10:05,050
A button, you know, Senator.

1239
02:10:05,060 --> 02:10:08,150
No, I don't know. Tell me.

1240
02:10:09,120 --> 02:10:11,850
When the boss says "push a button" on a guy,

1241
02:10:11,860 --> 02:10:13,350
I push a button.

1242
02:10:13,360 --> 02:10:14,710
See, Senator?

1243
02:10:14,720 --> 02:10:16,380
Mr. Questadt.

1244
02:10:16,510 --> 02:10:19,040
-You mean you kill people? -?

1245
02:10:19,050 --> 02:10:24,780
You kill people at the behest of your superiors.

1246
02:10:27,680 --> 02:10:29,290
Yeah, that's right.

1247
02:10:29,300 --> 02:10:34,720
And the head of your family is Michael Corleone?

1248
02:10:34,730 --> 02:10:37,920
Yeah, Counsellor. Michael Corleone.

1249
02:10:37,930 --> 02:10:39,520
Did you ever get such an order

1250
02:10:39,530 --> 02:10:41,520
directly from Michael Corleone?

1251
02:10:42,490 --> 02:10:44,680
No, I never talked to him.

1252
02:10:44,690 --> 02:10:46,290
Mr. Cicci

1253
02:10:46,380 --> 02:10:48,790
Could you amplify your answer a bit?

1254
02:10:49,080 --> 02:10:50,640
Do what?

1255
02:10:50,650 --> 02:10:52,900
Could you expand on your answer?

1256
02:10:52,910 --> 02:10:57,970
I'm particularly interested in knowing, was there always a buffer involved?

1257
02:10:58,110 --> 02:11:02,930
Someone in between you and your superiors who gave the order.

1258
02:11:02,940 --> 02:11:04,930
Right, a buffer.

1259
02:11:04,940 --> 02:11:07,200
The family had a lot of buffers!

1260
02:11:08,610 --> 02:11:10,630
You may find this very amusing,

1261
02:11:10,640 --> 02:11:13,730
but the members of this committee do not.

1262
02:11:48,090 --> 02:11:53,510
Tell me something, Ma.What did Papa think deep in his heart?

1263
02:11:57,920 --> 02:12:01,250
He was being strong.

1264
02:12:03,090 --> 02:12:09,730
Strong for his family.

1265
02:12:12,070 --> 02:12:20,860
But by being strong for his family

1266
02:12:22,110 --> 02:12:27,800
could he lose it?

1267
02:12:28,970 --> 02:12:32,430
You're thinking about your wife about the baby you lost.

1268
02:12:32,440 --> 02:12:40,740
But you and your wife can always have another baby.

1269
02:12:40,750 --> 02:12:46,920
No, I meant... lose his family,

1270
02:12:47,550 --> 02:12:54,310
But you can never lose your family.

1271
02:13:00,420 --> 02:13:02,810
Times are changing.

1272
02:13:24,500 --> 02:13:28,030
It's my pleasure. I don't want money.

1273
02:13:28,040 --> 02:13:31,620
-Take it as a gift.-

1274
02:13:31,630 --> 02:13:36,840
If there's something I can do for you, you come, we talk.

1275
02:13:37,300 --> 02:13:39,200
Grazie.

1276
02:13:53,080 --> 02:13:57,440
Signora Colombo, why did you come to see me?

1277
02:13:59,250 --> 02:14:05,510
Your wife told me to ask if you could help me.

1278
02:14:05,520 --> 02:14:08,210
She's in bad trouble.

1279
02:14:08,220 --> 02:14:12,410
Her neighbors complained to the landlord about her dog.

1280
02:14:13,550 --> 02:14:16,510
He told her to get rid of the animal.

1281
02:14:16,520 --> 02:14:20,050
But her little boy loves that dog.

1282
02:14:20,060 --> 02:14:22,620
So she hid it.

1283
02:14:22,630 --> 02:14:25,180
When the landlord found out

1284
02:14:25,190 --> 02:14:27,220
he got mad and told her to leave.

1285
02:14:27,230 --> 02:14:32,360
Now she can't stay even if she gets rid of it.

1286
02:14:32,370 --> 02:14:34,630
I'm so ashamed!

1287
02:14:34,640 --> 02:14:41,020
He said he'd get the police to throw us out on the street.

1288
02:14:41,840 --> 02:14:46,060
I'm sorry, but...

1289
02:14:46,070 --> 02:14:49,830
I could give you a couple dollars to help you move.

1290
02:14:49,840 --> 02:14:52,230
I can't move!

1291
02:14:52,410 --> 02:14:55,130
I want you to talk to him!

1292
02:14:55,140 --> 02:14:58,300
Tell him I want to stay here!

1293
02:15:05,640 --> 02:15:07,470
What's your landlord's name?

1294
02:15:07,480 --> 02:15:10,110
His name is Signor Roberto.

1295
02:15:10,120 --> 02:15:13,150
He lives on Fourth Street, near here.

1296
02:15:13,280 --> 02:15:17,010
They break the windows, they dirty the floors...

1297
02:15:17,020 --> 02:15:19,510
A real pig-sty, eh?

1298
02:15:31,230 --> 02:15:34,040
Mr.Roberto

1299
02:15:36,600 --> 02:15:39,550
My name is Vito Corleone.

1300
02:15:39,560 --> 02:15:42,960
Signora Colombo is a friend of my wife.

1301
02:15:42,970 --> 02:15:46,930
She says she's been evicted for no good reason.

1302
02:15:46,940 --> 02:15:50,890
She's a poor widow, she has nobody to take care of her.

1303
02:15:50,900 --> 02:15:54,130
She has no relatives,no money.

1304
02:15:54,140 --> 02:15:55,690
All she has is this neighborhood.

1305
02:15:55,700 --> 02:15:59,660
I already rented the place to another family.

1306
02:16:03,600 --> 02:16:06,960
I told her that I'd talk to you.

1307
02:16:06,970 --> 02:16:10,140
That you're a reasonable man.

1308
02:16:10,880 --> 02:16:14,870
She got rid of the animal that caused all the trouble.

1309
02:16:14,880 --> 02:16:17,730
So let her stay.

1310
02:16:19,780 --> 02:16:23,250
-Are you Sicilian?-No, I'm Calabrese.

1311
02:16:23,720 --> 02:16:27,410
We're practically paesani, do me this favor.

1312
02:16:27,420 --> 02:16:32,380
I already rented it! I'll look like an idiot.

1313
02:16:32,390 --> 02:16:34,280
Besides, the new tenants pay more rent.

1314
02:16:34,290 --> 02:16:37,080
How much more a month?

1315
02:16:37,090 --> 02:16:39,650
Five bucks.

1316
02:16:43,730 --> 02:16:46,290
Here's six months increase in advance.

1317
02:16:46,460 --> 02:16:50,680
But don't tell her about it. She's very proud.

1318
02:16:50,690 --> 02:16:53,690
Come see me in another six months.

1319
02:16:55,160 --> 02:16:58,260
Of course, the dog stays. Right?

1320
02:16:59,000 --> 02:17:00,520
The dog stays.

1321
02:17:00,530 --> 02:17:08,300
Who the hell are you to come give me orders?

1322
02:17:08,310 --> 02:17:14,800
Watch out or I'll kick your Sicilian ass right into the street!

1323
02:17:14,810 --> 02:17:20,560
Do me this favor.I won't forget it.

1324
02:17:20,570 --> 02:17:24,900
Ask your friends in the neighborhood about me.

1325
02:17:24,910 --> 02:17:32,520
They'll tell you I know how to return a favor.

1326
02:17:34,150 --> 02:17:37,070
What a character!

1327
02:17:43,150 --> 02:17:46,520
That landlord is here... Roberto

1328
02:17:46,530 --> 02:17:49,510
the one who owns those ratholes.

1329
02:17:57,290 --> 02:18:01,050
He's been asking all around the neighborhood about you.

1330
02:18:03,260 --> 02:18:05,220
Grazie.

1331
02:18:07,330 --> 02:18:11,960
I hope I'm not disturbing you, Don Vito.

1332
02:18:11,970 --> 02:18:15,060
What can I do for you, Don Roberto?

1333
02:18:15,200 --> 02:18:19,300
What a misunderstanding! Holy Mary!

1334
02:18:19,440 --> 02:18:24,960
Of course Signora Colombo can stay!

1335
02:18:25,340 --> 02:18:27,430
Grazie...

1336
02:18:27,440 --> 02:18:33,500
I'm giving back the money you gave me.

1337
02:18:33,510 --> 02:18:39,970
Un, due, three, four, five, six, tutt'!

1338
02:18:39,980 --> 02:18:45,710
Because after all, Don Vito, money isn't everything.

1339
02:18:53,390 --> 02:18:55,210
Can I sit down?

1340
02:18:56,320 --> 02:18:57,970
Grazie.

1341
02:18:57,980 --> 02:19:01,820
Your kindness to that widow made me ashamed of myself.

1342
02:19:01,830 --> 02:19:05,650
The rent stays like before!

1343
02:19:13,230 --> 02:19:18,770
I'll even lower it.

1344
02:19:19,190 --> 02:19:22,300
I'll lower it $5.

1345
02:19:24,600 --> 02:19:26,820
I'll lower it $10!

1346
02:19:26,830 --> 02:19:30,900
Grazie...

1347
02:19:30,910 --> 02:19:35,190
Can I offer you some coffee?

1348
02:19:35,200 --> 02:19:40,730
I'm late for an appointment!

1349
02:19:40,740 --> 02:19:44,970
I can't this time! Ask me another time!

1350
02:19:44,980 --> 02:19:51,970
You'll have to excuse me for now.

1351
02:19:52,280 --> 02:20:00,670
I wish I could stay longer!

1352
02:20:00,680 --> 02:20:07,150
Just call me and I'll be here!

1353
02:20:07,160 --> 02:20:12,780
Grazie.

1354
02:20:15,950 --> 02:20:20,240
He won't be back. He'll hide out in the Bronx!

1355
02:20:34,800 --> 02:20:37,390
Vito, what do you think?

1356
02:20:37,400 --> 02:20:39,720
We'll make a big business!

1357
02:20:46,910 --> 02:20:49,760
-New York City.-We'll make a big business!

1358
02:20:50,310 --> 02:20:52,100
New York City.

1359
02:20:52,110 --> 02:20:55,870
- Are you the son of Vito Corleone? - Yes, I am.

1360
02:20:55,910 --> 02:20:57,660
Where was he born?

1361
02:20:57,670 --> 02:20:59,440
Corleone, Sicily.

1362
02:20:59,450 --> 02:21:01,740
Did he at times use an alias

1363
02:21:01,750 --> 02:21:05,770
that was known in certain circles as Godfather?

1364
02:21:06,310 --> 02:21:09,870
Godfather is a term used by his friends.

1365
02:21:09,880 --> 02:21:13,110
One of affection and respect.

1366
02:21:13,120 --> 02:21:14,480
Mr. Chairman

1367
02:21:14,490 --> 02:21:17,840
I would like to verify the witness' statement.

1368
02:21:17,850 --> 02:21:22,910
For years many of my constituents have been of Italian descent.

1369
02:21:23,130 --> 02:21:25,450
I've come to know them well.

1370
02:21:25,830 --> 02:21:30,210
They have honoured me with their support and their friendship.

1371
02:21:30,220 --> 02:21:31,680
I can proudly say

1372
02:21:31,690 --> 02:21:36,120
that some of my very best friends are Italian-Americans.

1373
02:21:36,590 --> 02:21:41,750
However, Mr. Chairman, unfortunately I have to leave these proceedings

1374
02:21:41,760 --> 02:21:44,550
in order to preside over a very important meeting

1375
02:21:44,560 --> 02:21:46,730
of my own committee.

1376
02:21:46,800 --> 02:21:50,160
Before I leave, I do want to say this

1377
02:21:50,170 --> 02:21:54,660
that these hearings on the Mafia are in no way whatsoever

1378
02:21:54,670 --> 02:21:57,290
a slur upon the great Italian people.

1379
02:21:57,300 --> 02:22:00,590
I can state from my own knowledge and experience

1380
02:22:00,600 --> 02:22:05,830
that Italian-Americans are among the most loyal,most law-abiding,

1381
02:22:05,840 --> 02:22:10,130
patriotic, hard-working American citizens in this land.

1382
02:22:10,380 --> 02:22:15,440
It would be a shame, Mr. Chairman

1383
02:22:15,450 --> 02:22:18,100
if we allowed a few rotten apples to give a bad nameto the whole barrel.

1384
02:22:18,110 --> 02:22:20,870
ecause from the time of Christopher Columbus

1385
02:22:20,880 --> 02:22:23,550
to the time of Enrico Fermi

1386
02:22:23,560 --> 02:22:30,540
Italian-Americans have been pioneers in building and defending our nation.

1387
02:22:30,550 --> 02:22:32,410
They are the salt of the earth

1388
02:22:32,420 --> 02:22:35,520
and one of the backbones of this country.

1389
02:22:38,320 --> 02:22:39,450
Here,

1390
02:22:39,460 --> 02:22:41,780
Here...

1391
02:22:41,790 --> 02:22:45,420
I think we all agree with our esteemed college.

1392
02:22:45,560 --> 02:22:46,710
Now,Mr. Corleone

1393
02:22:46,720 --> 02:22:49,820
you have been advised as to your legal rights.

1394
02:22:50,060 --> 02:22:52,080
We have testimony

1395
02:22:52,090 --> 02:22:53,350
from a previous witness

1396
02:22:53,360 --> 02:22:56,260
one Willi Cicci.

1397
02:22:56,560 --> 02:22:57,990
He stated hat you are head of

1398
02:22:58,000 --> 02:23:00,990
the most powerful Mafia family in the country.

1399
02:23:01,000 --> 02:23:03,390
- Are you? - No, I'm not.

1400
02:23:03,400 --> 02:23:06,920
He testified that you are personally responsible

1401
02:23:06,930 --> 02:23:12,290
for the murder of a New York police captain in 1947

1402
02:23:12,300 --> 02:23:14,500
and with him a man named Virgil Sollozzo.

1403
02:23:14,510 --> 02:23:17,130
- Do you deny this? - Yes, I do.

1404
02:23:17,140 --> 02:23:22,340
Is it true that in the year 1950 you devised the murder

1405
02:23:22,350 --> 02:23:26,000
of the heads of the "Five Families" in New York

1406
02:23:26,010 --> 02:23:29,680
who assume and consolidate your nefarious power?

1407
02:23:29,690 --> 02:23:31,940
It's a complete falsehood.

1408
02:23:31,950 --> 02:23:33,210
Mr. Questadt.

1409
02:23:33,220 --> 02:23:38,100
Is it true you have a controlling interest in three major hotels in Las Vegas?

1410
02:23:38,720 --> 02:23:39,940
No, it's not true.

1411
02:23:39,950 --> 02:23:42,640
I own some stock in some of the hotels there

1412
02:23:42,650 --> 02:23:44,250
but very little.

1413
02:23:46,760 --> 02:23:51,040
I also have stock in IBM and IT&T.

1414
02:23:51,050 --> 02:23:52,180
Mr. Corleone

1415
02:23:52,190 --> 02:23:56,480
Mr. Corleone do you have any interests or control over gambling or narcotics

1416
02:23:56,490 --> 02:23:59,820
-in the state of New York.? -No, I do not.

1417
02:23:59,830 --> 02:24:02,410
Senator, my client would like

1418
02:24:02,420 --> 02:24:03,620
to read a statement.

1419
02:24:03,630 --> 02:24:04,820
Mr. Chairman

1420
02:24:04,830 --> 02:24:07,190
Mr. Chairman,I think this statement is

1421
02:24:07,200 --> 02:24:09,390
totally out of order at this time.

1422
02:24:09,400 --> 02:24:12,430
Sir, my client has answered

1423
02:24:12,440 --> 02:24:13,690
this committee's questions with sincerity.

1424
02:24:13,700 --> 02:24:17,260
He hasn't taken

1425
02:24:17,270 --> 02:24:18,800
the Fifth Amendment

1426
02:24:18,810 --> 02:24:20,130
so this statement

1427
02:24:20,140 --> 02:24:21,960
should be heard!

1428
02:24:23,210 --> 02:24:26,700
No, I'll allow Mr. Corleone to read his statement.

1429
02:24:26,710 --> 02:24:28,770
I'll put it in the record.

1430
02:24:30,010 --> 02:24:32,910
In the hopes of clearing my family name

1431
02:24:33,040 --> 02:24:35,400
to give my children their

1432
02:24:35,410 --> 02:24:37,300
share of the American way of life

1433
02:24:37,310 --> 02:24:40,140
without a blemish on their name and background

1434
02:24:40,350 --> 02:24:45,870
I have appeared before this committee and given it all my cooperation.

1435
02:24:46,890 --> 02:24:52,510
I consider it a great personal dishonour to have to deny that I am a criminal.

1436
02:24:53,480 --> 02:24:56,480
I wish to have the following noted for the record:

1437
02:24:56,950 --> 02:24:58,810
That I served my country faithfully

1438
02:24:58,820 --> 02:25:01,280
in World War Two and was awarded

1439
02:25:01,290 --> 02:25:03,640
the Navy Cross for actions

1440
02:25:03,650 --> 02:25:06,350
in defence of my country.

1441
02:25:07,130 --> 02:25:11,420
That I have never been arrested or indicted for any crime.

1442
02:25:11,460 --> 02:25:15,390
That no proof linking me to any criminal conspiracy

1443
02:25:15,690 --> 02:25:18,760
whether it is called Mafia or Cosa Nostra

1444
02:25:18,770 --> 02:25:22,890
or any other name has ever been made public.

1445
02:25:23,060 --> 02:25:26,130
I have not taken refuge behind the Fifth Amendment

1446
02:25:26,140 --> 02:25:28,330
although I may do so.

1447
02:25:31,170 --> 02:25:33,420
I challenge this committee

1448
02:25:33,430 --> 02:25:36,700
to produce any witness or evidence against me

1449
02:25:36,940 --> 02:25:38,830
and if they do not

1450
02:25:39,370 --> 02:25:41,560
I hope they will have the decency

1451
02:25:41,570 --> 02:25:44,800
to clear my name with the same publicity

1452
02:25:44,810 --> 02:25:47,300
with which they have besmirched it.

1453
02:25:48,040 --> 02:25:50,840
I'm sure we're all quite impressed.

1454
02:25:50,850 --> 02:25:53,340
Particularly with your love for our country.

1455
02:25:53,550 --> 02:25:56,430
We'll be in recess until 10 a.m. Monday

1456
02:25:56,440 --> 02:25:58,770
when we will produce a witness

1457
02:25:58,780 --> 02:26:01,410
who'll corroborate the charges against you.

1458
02:26:01,420 --> 02:26:03,040
And at which time Mr.Corleone.

1459
02:26:03,050 --> 02:26:06,440
you may very well be subject to indictment for perjury.

1460
02:26:06,450 --> 02:26:11,270
I remind you that you're still under subpoena.Adjourned!

1461
02:26:14,960 --> 02:26:17,750
Ten-to-one shot, you said.

1462
02:26:17,760 --> 02:26:19,450
Ten-to-one shot

1463
02:26:19,460 --> 02:26:22,780
He would take the Fifth, and I lose.

1464
02:26:22,790 --> 02:26:24,950
You sound like my bookie.

1465
02:26:24,960 --> 02:26:27,390
I owe that monkey my life.

1466
02:26:28,570 --> 02:26:30,420
Well, just get a good night's sleep.

1467
02:26:30,430 --> 02:26:32,020
Yeah.

1468
02:26:32,030 --> 02:26:34,160
You've got a big day tomorrow.

1469
02:26:34,330 --> 02:26:38,330
I've got you a new suit, new shirt, new tie.

1470
02:26:38,740 --> 02:26:41,500
I'll shave you myself in the morning.

1471
02:26:42,140 --> 02:26:44,160
You'll look respectable for 50 million

1472
02:26:44,170 --> 02:26:46,230
of your fellow Americans.

1473
02:26:46,240 --> 02:26:51,670
Tomorrow... My life won't be worth a nickel after tomorrow.

1474
02:26:52,510 --> 02:26:56,600
Come on! I saw this 19 times.

1475
02:26:57,310 --> 02:26:59,770
You've got a great home here

1476
02:26:59,950 --> 02:27:02,140
for the rest of your life.Nobody gets near you

1477
02:27:02,150 --> 02:27:03,810
you're not going anywhere.

1478
02:27:03,950 --> 02:27:07,110
That's great. Beautiful.

1479
02:27:07,350 --> 02:27:09,480
Some deal I made.

1480
02:27:09,490 --> 02:27:12,270
You'll live like a king. You'll be a hero.

1481
02:27:12,280 --> 02:27:15,370
You'll live better here than most people outside.

1482
02:27:15,380 --> 02:27:17,050
Some deal!

1483
02:27:21,620 --> 02:27:24,720
Alive. Pentangeli is alive.

1484
02:27:25,980 --> 02:27:27,880
How did they get their hands on him?

1485
02:27:27,890 --> 02:27:32,020
Roth. He engineered it, Michael.

1486
02:27:32,030 --> 02:27:34,580
When Frankie went to make a deal with the Rosato brothers

1487
02:27:34,590 --> 02:27:36,580
they tried to kill him.

1488
02:27:36,590 --> 02:27:38,760
He thought you double-crossed him.

1489
02:27:40,030 --> 02:27:42,790
Our people with the detectives said he was half dead

1490
02:27:42,800 --> 02:27:45,890
scared,and shouted that you'd turned on him.

1491
02:27:46,200 --> 02:27:47,790
They already had him on possession

1492
02:27:47,800 --> 02:27:51,230
bookmaking, murder one and more.

1493
02:27:52,330 --> 02:27:55,260
The FBI has him airtight.

1494
02:27:55,270 --> 02:27:58,100
He's on an army base, 24 hour guards.

1495
02:27:58,110 --> 02:28:01,130
We can't get to him.

1496
02:28:01,140 --> 02:28:03,570
You've opened yourself to five counts of perjury.

1497
02:28:05,540 --> 02:28:08,570
What about Fredo? What does he know?

1498
02:28:08,580 --> 02:28:10,200
He says he doesn't know anything

1499
02:28:10,210 --> 02:28:11,950
and I believe him.

1500
02:28:12,480 --> 02:28:17,380
Roth, he... played this one beautifully.

1501
02:28:24,290 --> 02:28:26,210
I'm going to talk to Fredo.

1502
02:29:06,100 --> 02:29:08,770
I haven't got a lot to say, Mike.

1503
02:29:10,410 --> 02:29:12,440
We have time.

1504
02:29:13,080 --> 02:29:16,300
I was kept pretty much in the dark.

1505
02:29:17,540 --> 02:29:19,700
I didn't know all that much.

1506
02:29:20,610 --> 02:29:22,430
What about now?

1507
02:29:23,450 --> 02:29:28,770
Is there anything you can help me out with? Anything you can tell me now?

1508
02:29:30,310 --> 02:29:33,340
They've got Pentangeli.

1509
02:29:47,550 --> 02:29:50,750
I didn't know it was going to be a hit, Mike.

1510
02:29:51,360 --> 02:29:54,550
I swear to God I didn't know.

1511
02:29:56,560 --> 02:29:59,080
Johnny Ola bumped into me

1512
02:29:59,090 --> 02:30:01,260
in Beverly Hills.

1513
02:30:02,760 --> 02:30:05,930
He said that he wanted to talk.

1514
02:30:07,400 --> 02:30:14,570
He said that you and Roth were in on a big deal together.

1515
02:30:16,040 --> 02:30:20,360
And that there was something in it for me if I could help him out.

1516
02:30:20,370 --> 02:30:24,460
He said that you were being tough on the negotiations

1517
02:30:24,470 --> 02:30:26,730
but if they could get a little help

1518
02:30:26,740 --> 02:30:29,330
and close the deal fast

1519
02:30:30,380 --> 02:30:33,730
it would be good for the family.

1520
02:30:34,440 --> 02:30:36,810
And you believed that story?

1521
02:30:37,410 --> 02:30:39,200
You believed that?

1522
02:30:39,210 --> 02:30:41,770
He said there was something in it for me

1523
02:30:41,780 --> 02:30:45,510
-on my own! -I've always taken care of you, Fredo.

1524
02:30:45,590 --> 02:30:47,810
Taken care of me?!

1525
02:30:48,650 --> 02:30:52,210
You're my kid brother!You take care of me?

1526
02:30:52,450 --> 02:30:54,280
Did you ever think about that?

1527
02:30:54,290 --> 02:30:57,490
Did you ever once think about that?

1528
02:30:57,690 --> 02:30:59,150
Send Fredo off to do this

1529
02:30:59,160 --> 02:31:01,650
send Fredo off to do that!

1530
02:31:02,460 --> 02:31:07,050
Let Fredo take care of some Mickey Mouse nightclub somewhere.

1531
02:31:07,060 --> 02:31:10,320
Let Fredo fetch somebody at the airport!

1532
02:31:10,330 --> 02:31:11,850
I'm your older brother

1533
02:31:11,860 --> 02:31:13,590
but was stepped over!

1534
02:31:13,600 --> 02:31:17,090
- It's the way Pop wanted it.- It's not the way I wanted it!

1535
02:31:18,000 --> 02:31:20,920
I can handle things, I'm smart!

1536
02:31:20,930 --> 02:31:23,990
Not like everybody says.

1537
02:31:24,000 --> 02:31:27,170
Like dumb. I'm smart and I want respect!

1538
02:31:34,870 --> 02:31:38,670
Is there anything you can tell me about this investigation?

1539
02:31:38,680 --> 02:31:40,560
Anything more?

1540
02:31:47,940 --> 02:31:54,900
The senate lawyer, Questadt... He belongs to Roth.

1541
02:32:03,790 --> 02:32:05,350
Fredo...

1542
02:32:07,850 --> 02:32:10,210
...you're nothing to me now.

1543
02:32:12,430 --> 02:32:16,450
Not a brother, not a friend.

1544
02:32:16,520 --> 02:32:19,520
I don't want to know you, or what you do.

1545
02:32:20,890 --> 02:32:23,160
I don't want to see you at the hotels.

1546
02:32:23,860 --> 02:32:26,630
I don't want you near my house.

1547
02:32:28,360 --> 02:32:33,420
When you see our mother, I want to know in advance, so I won't be there.

1548
02:32:34,560 --> 02:32:36,620
You understand?

1549
02:32:46,170 --> 02:32:48,200
Mikey.

1550
02:32:54,510 --> 02:32:58,940
I don't want anything to happen to him while my mother's alive.

1551
02:33:48,830 --> 02:33:51,500
There's more people than at a ballgame in here.

1552
02:33:52,200 --> 02:33:54,700
Hey, there's Willi Cicci!

1553
02:34:16,110 --> 02:34:18,880
This committee will come to order!

1554
02:34:21,220 --> 02:34:22,710
State your name, please.

1555
02:34:22,720 --> 02:34:24,240
Frank Pentangeli.

1556
02:34:24,250 --> 02:34:25,410
Where were you born?

1557
02:34:25,420 --> 02:34:27,970
Pontenegro, it's outside of Palermo.

1558
02:34:27,980 --> 02:34:29,770
Where do you live now?

1559
02:34:30,250 --> 02:34:35,040
I live in an army barracks with the FBI guys.

1560
02:34:36,420 --> 02:34:39,080
We have here a witness

1561
02:34:39,090 --> 02:34:42,280
that will further testify,to Michael Corleone's

1562
02:34:42,290 --> 02:34:44,420
rule of a criminal empire

1563
02:34:44,430 --> 02:34:47,890
that controls all gambling.

1564
02:34:47,900 --> 02:34:49,920
This witness has had no buffer

1565
02:34:49,930 --> 02:34:52,650
between himself and Michael Corleone.

1566
02:34:52,660 --> 02:34:53,920
He can corroborate enough charges

1567
02:34:53,930 --> 02:34:55,850
for us to recommend

1568
02:34:55,860 --> 02:34:56,920
a charge of perjury

1569
02:34:56,930 --> 02:35:00,930
against Michael Corleone.

1570
02:35:00,940 --> 02:35:03,530
- Senator. - Thank you, Chairman.

1571
02:35:04,240 --> 02:35:06,390
Mr. Pentangeli...

1572
02:35:07,140 --> 02:35:09,370
Mr. Pentangeli.

1573
02:35:09,570 --> 02:35:12,600
Were you a member of the Corleone family?

1574
02:35:12,810 --> 02:35:18,000
Did you serve under Caporegime, Peter Clemenza,

1575
02:35:18,010 --> 02:35:22,710
and under Vito Corleone,also known as the Godfather?

1576
02:35:28,350 --> 02:35:31,620
I never knew any Godfather.

1577
02:35:33,520 --> 02:35:36,370
I have my own family.

1578
02:35:39,020 --> 02:35:41,110
Mr. Pentangeli, you...

1579
02:35:41,490 --> 02:35:43,680
You are contradicting

1580
02:35:43,690 --> 02:35:46,310
your own sworn statement.

1581
02:35:46,320 --> 02:35:48,150
I ask you again, sir

1582
02:35:48,160 --> 02:35:49,880
here and now under oath,

1583
02:35:49,890 --> 02:35:56,250
were you at any time a member of a crime organisation led by Michael Corleone?

1584
02:35:56,260 --> 02:35:58,320
I don't know nothing about that!

1585
02:36:02,090 --> 02:36:06,090
I was in the olive oil business with his father

1586
02:36:06,200 --> 02:36:09,590
but that was a long time ago.

1587
02:36:10,030 --> 02:36:13,190
We have a sworn affidavit.

1588
02:36:13,190 --> 02:36:16,290
Your sworn affidavit

1589
02:36:16,300 --> 02:36:19,430
that you murdered on the orders of Michael Corleone.

1590
02:36:19,440 --> 02:36:21,400
Do you deny this confession

1591
02:36:21,410 --> 02:36:24,190
and do you realise what will happen if you do?

1592
02:36:24,200 --> 02:36:27,330
The FBI guys promised me a deal

1593
02:36:27,340 --> 02:36:31,240
so I made up a lot of stuff about Michael Corleone

1594
02:36:31,250 --> 02:36:33,270
just to please them.

1595
02:36:33,280 --> 02:36:35,570
But it was all lies.

1596
02:36:35,640 --> 02:36:38,100
Everything!

1597
02:36:38,110 --> 02:36:42,940
They kept saying,"Michael Corleone did this"

1598
02:36:42,950 --> 02:36:46,010
and "Michael Corleone did that".

1599
02:36:46,790 --> 02:36:51,110
So I said, "Yeah, sure. Why not?"

1600
02:36:51,120 --> 02:36:52,600
Mr. Corleone

1601
02:36:52,610 --> 02:36:55,240
would you kindly identify

1602
02:36:55,250 --> 02:36:57,310
the gentleman sitting to your left?

1603
02:36:57,320 --> 02:36:59,020
I can answer that.

1604
02:36:59,660 --> 02:37:02,780
His name is Vincenzo Pentangeli.

1605
02:37:02,920 --> 02:37:05,210
Is he related to the witness?

1606
02:37:05,590 --> 02:37:07,620
He is, I believe, his brother.

1607
02:37:07,830 --> 02:37:10,210
Will he come forward and be sworn?

1608
02:37:10,260 --> 02:37:12,660
He doesn't understand English.

1609
02:37:12,670 --> 02:37:13,780
He came at his own expense

1610
02:37:13,790 --> 02:37:16,320
to aid his brother.

1611
02:37:16,330 --> 02:37:19,090
He's not under subpoena,and his reputation in his own country

1612
02:37:19,100 --> 02:37:20,220
is impeccable.

1613
02:37:20,230 --> 02:37:22,090
He knows nothing about this?

1614
02:37:22,100 --> 02:37:24,060
To my knowledge, nothing.

1615
02:37:24,070 --> 02:37:26,820
I'm going to find out what happened!

1616
02:37:26,830 --> 02:37:29,150
This committee is now adjourned.

1617
02:37:29,160 --> 02:37:30,390
The witness is excused.

1618
02:37:30,400 --> 02:37:31,800
Senator!

1619
02:37:32,210 --> 02:37:33,360
Senator!

1620
02:37:33,370 --> 02:37:36,070
This committee owes an apology!

1621
02:37:36,380 --> 02:37:40,730
This committee owes an apology. Apology, Senator!

1622
02:38:07,920 --> 02:38:12,480
- Michael, excuse me. - Hello, darling.

1623
02:38:12,490 --> 02:38:15,250
The children are outside. We're going.

1624
02:38:17,220 --> 02:38:20,180
What do you mean? We're leaving tomorrow.

1625
02:38:21,060 --> 02:38:26,530
-Rocco?-I'll be in my room, Mike.

1626
02:38:29,530 --> 02:38:32,230
Michael, I'm not going back to Nevada.

1627
02:38:32,600 --> 02:38:35,790
I brought the children to say goodbye to you.

1628
02:38:39,200 --> 02:38:41,920
I'm very happy for you.

1629
02:38:41,930 --> 02:38:44,620
I always knew you were too smart

1630
02:38:44,630 --> 02:38:47,130
to let any of them beat you.

1631
02:38:47,910 --> 02:38:52,570
- Why don't you sit down? - No, I'm not going to stay long.

1632
02:38:52,580 --> 02:38:54,870
There are some things I'd like to talk to you about.

1633
02:38:56,880 --> 02:38:59,260
Things that have been on my mind

1634
02:39:00,220 --> 02:39:01,800
changes I want to make.

1635
02:39:01,810 --> 02:39:05,080
I think it's too late for changes, Michael.

1636
02:39:05,950 --> 02:39:08,410
I wasn't going to say anything...

1637
02:39:08,420 --> 02:39:10,980
-but now...- What do you mean, "too late"?

1638
02:39:16,020 --> 02:39:19,440
What really happened with Pentangeli?

1639
02:39:24,660 --> 02:39:26,850
His brother came and helped him.

1640
02:39:26,890 --> 02:39:29,020
I didn't even know he had a brother.

1641
02:39:29,860 --> 02:39:31,680
Where is he now?

1642
02:39:32,990 --> 02:39:36,160
He's on a plane, back to Sicily.

1643
02:39:36,460 --> 02:39:39,130
All he had to do was show his face.

1644
02:39:40,630 --> 02:39:43,230
It was between the brothers, Kay.

1645
02:39:43,500 --> 02:39:45,850
I had nothing to do with it.

1646
02:39:53,300 --> 02:39:56,500
Don't tell me you're going, Not you, not the kids

1647
02:39:56,510 --> 02:40:00,560
No,You're my wife and my children

1648
02:40:00,570 --> 02:40:02,600
I love you and won't allow it

1649
02:40:02,940 --> 02:40:06,930
You say you love me, but talk about allowing me to leave!

1650
02:40:06,940 --> 02:40:09,630
That have been going on for years between mean and women

1651
02:40:09,640 --> 02:40:10,730
that will not change an that's it.

1652
02:40:10,740 --> 02:40:13,200
-You've become blind! -Blind to what?

1653
02:40:13,210 --> 02:40:14,900
Look what's happened to us.

1654
02:40:14,910 --> 02:40:16,100
Mike!my God,

1655
02:40:16,110 --> 02:40:18,210
Look what's happened to our son, Michael.

1656
02:40:18,220 --> 02:40:19,940
-Nothing's happened to him. -Don't tell me nothing's...

1657
02:40:19,950 --> 02:40:21,710
-Anthony's fine. -Anthony's not fine!

1658
02:40:21,720 --> 02:40:23,210
-I don't wanna hear about it. -You will hear about it!

1659
02:40:23,220 --> 02:40:24,840
-I don't wanna hear about it! -Anthony's friends...

1660
02:40:24,850 --> 02:40:26,380
- I don't want to hear about it.- are your buttonmen!

1661
02:40:26,390 --> 02:40:28,350
I don't want to hear about it!

1662
02:40:29,290 --> 02:40:31,080
Over!

1663
02:40:43,660 --> 02:40:48,290
At this moment I feel no love for you at all.

1664
02:40:48,330 --> 02:40:51,520
I never thought that would ever happen

1665
02:40:51,830 --> 02:40:54,500
but it has.

1666
02:41:07,540 --> 02:41:09,170
Kay...

1667
02:41:12,770 --> 02:41:14,690
We're leaving tomorrow.

1668
02:41:15,340 --> 02:41:18,530
Why don't you take the kids back to their room?

1669
02:41:18,540 --> 02:41:20,760
Michael, you haven't heard me.

1670
02:41:20,770 --> 02:41:24,440
Kay, what do you want from me?

1671
02:41:24,810 --> 02:41:27,270
Do you expect me to let you go

1672
02:41:27,280 --> 02:41:31,870
to let you take my children from me?

1673
02:41:31,880 --> 02:41:33,210
Don't you know me?

1674
02:41:33,220 --> 02:41:35,240
Don't you know that

1675
02:41:35,250 --> 02:41:37,540
that's an impossibility?

1676
02:41:37,550 --> 02:41:42,010
That I'd use all my power to keep that from happening?

1677
02:41:42,150 --> 02:41:44,780
Don't you know that?

1678
02:41:46,260 --> 02:41:47,950
Kay..

1679
02:41:51,320 --> 02:41:53,460
In time

1680
02:41:54,190 --> 02:41:56,430
you'll feel differently.

1681
02:41:57,320 --> 02:42:00,190
You'll be glad I stopped you now.

1682
02:42:02,100 --> 02:42:03,980
I know that.

1683
02:42:06,100 --> 02:42:09,360
I know you blame me for losing the baby.

1684
02:42:11,230 --> 02:42:16,200
I know what that meant to you.

1685
02:42:18,610 --> 02:42:20,870
I'll make it up to you, Kay.

1686
02:42:21,440 --> 02:42:24,370
I swear I'll make it up to you. I'll...

1687
02:42:25,600 --> 02:42:27,840
I'm going to change.

1688
02:42:28,870 --> 02:42:30,760
I'll change.

1689
02:42:30,770 --> 02:42:34,630
I've learned that I have the strength to change.

1690
02:42:35,350 --> 02:42:38,270
Then you'll forget about this miscarriage...

1691
02:42:39,180 --> 02:42:41,370
...and we'll have another child.

1692
02:42:41,380 --> 02:42:43,070
And we'll go on, you and I.

1693
02:42:43,080 --> 02:42:46,670
We'll go on.

1694
02:42:47,990 --> 02:42:50,400
Oh, Michael!

1695
02:42:50,690 --> 02:42:53,280
Michael, you are blind.

1696
02:42:54,690 --> 02:43:01,620
It wasn't a miscarriage.It was an abortion.

1697
02:43:02,590 --> 02:43:08,650
An abortion, Michael. Just like our marriage is an abortion.

1698
02:43:08,660 --> 02:43:12,790
Something that's unholy and evil!

1699
02:43:13,600 --> 02:43:16,790
I didn't want your son, Michael!

1700
02:43:17,020 --> 02:43:21,660
I wouldn't bring another one of your sons into this world!

1701
02:43:22,630 --> 02:43:25,190
It was an abortion, Michael.

1702
02:43:25,200 --> 02:43:28,320
It was a son and I had it killed

1703
02:43:28,330 --> 02:43:31,660
because this must all end!

1704
02:43:32,400 --> 02:43:35,160
I know now that it's over.

1705
02:43:35,170 --> 02:43:37,490
I knew it then.

1706
02:43:37,870 --> 02:43:40,360
There would be no way, Michael

1707
02:43:40,370 --> 02:43:43,470
no way you could ever forgive me.

1708
02:43:43,480 --> 02:43:48,940
Not with this Sicilian thing that's been going on for 2,000...

1709
02:43:55,880 --> 02:43:59,310
- You won't take my children. - I will.

1710
02:43:59,320 --> 02:44:04,070
- You won't take my children! - They're my children too.

1711
02:45:46,230 --> 02:45:49,630
Hey,Sonny.what you doing,don't make a fight.

1712
02:47:45,090 --> 02:47:46,980
Ciccio

1713
02:47:47,090 --> 02:47:48,910
Don Ciccio

1714
02:47:51,390 --> 02:47:53,620
Don Ciccio

1715
02:47:54,130 --> 02:47:55,820
Don Ciccio, it's Tommasino.

1716
02:47:55,830 --> 02:47:59,950
Allow me the honor of introducing someone.

1717
02:47:59,960 --> 02:48:02,820
My partner in America, in New York.

1718
02:48:02,830 --> 02:48:06,750
His name is Vito Corleone.

1719
02:48:06,760 --> 02:48:10,220
We'll send him olive oil from here.

1720
02:48:10,230 --> 02:48:16,560
To his company in America.

1721
02:48:16,570 --> 02:48:20,310
They're olive oil importers, Don Ciccio.

1722
02:48:28,540 --> 02:48:32,630
We'd like your blessing

1723
02:48:32,640 --> 02:48:35,910
and your permission to start work.

1724
02:48:36,240 --> 02:48:40,310
Where is this young man from New York?

1725
02:48:42,310 --> 02:48:46,470
Have him come closer.

1726
02:48:46,480 --> 02:48:50,410
I can't see him so good.

1727
02:48:56,560 --> 02:48:58,410
My respects, Don Ciccio.

1728
02:48:58,420 --> 02:49:00,050
Give me your blessing.

1729
02:49:02,590 --> 02:49:04,480
Bless you!

1730
02:49:06,600 --> 02:49:08,620
What's your name?

1731
02:49:08,630 --> 02:49:10,380
Vito Corleone.

1732
02:49:10,390 --> 02:49:12,550
Vito Corleone.

1733
02:49:13,300 --> 02:49:16,920
You took the name of this town!

1734
02:49:16,930 --> 02:49:19,190
And what's your father's name?

1735
02:49:19,200 --> 02:49:23,260
His name was... Antonio Andolini.

1736
02:49:23,270 --> 02:49:28,400
Louder, I don't hear so good.

1737
02:49:29,970 --> 02:49:33,530
My father's name was Antonio Andolini...

1738
02:49:33,540 --> 02:49:36,700
...and this is for you!

1739
02:50:58,040 --> 02:51:00,740
Michael, say goodbye.

1740
02:52:03,640 --> 02:52:05,310
Hi, Al.

1741
02:52:16,210 --> 02:52:19,950
Can I speak with you for a second, Tom?

1742
02:52:28,080 --> 02:52:29,750
Tom, where's Mike?

1743
02:52:30,950 --> 02:52:33,050
Waiting for you to leave.

1744
02:52:35,690 --> 02:52:37,620
Can I talk with him?

1745
02:52:37,830 --> 02:52:40,060
Sorry, Fredo. No chance.

1746
02:52:40,620 --> 02:52:44,380
- Can I see him? - He's in the boathouse.

1747
02:52:57,230 --> 02:52:59,660
Michael, it's Connie.

1748
02:53:20,840 --> 02:53:22,580
Michael

1749
02:53:25,340 --> 02:53:29,510
I'd like to stay close to home now, if it's all right.

1750
02:53:37,410 --> 02:53:39,080
Is Kay coming?

1751
02:53:42,420 --> 02:53:44,050
No.

1752
02:53:51,490 --> 02:53:54,590
Fredo's in the house with Mama.

1753
02:53:54,790 --> 02:53:59,790
He asked for you and Tom said you wouldn't see him.

1754
02:54:02,360 --> 02:54:04,530
That's right.

1755
02:54:07,100 --> 02:54:10,690
Kids, why don't you go outside for a while?

1756
02:54:14,170 --> 02:54:17,400
Please, I want to talk to you.

1757
02:54:27,880 --> 02:54:32,530
Michael, I hated you for so many years.

1758
02:54:32,540 --> 02:54:36,360
I think I did things to myself, to hurt myself

1759
02:54:36,370 --> 02:54:43,800
so that you'd know that I could hurt you.

1760
02:54:49,290 --> 02:54:54,020
You were just being strong for all of us,the way Papa was.

1761
02:54:54,150 --> 02:54:56,210
And I forgive you.

1762
02:55:00,520 --> 02:55:03,250
Can't you forgive Fredo?

1763
02:55:03,630 --> 02:55:05,850
He's so sweet

1764
02:55:05,860 --> 02:55:08,860
and helpless without you.

1765
02:55:14,730 --> 02:55:16,280
You need me.

1766
02:55:16,290 --> 02:55:19,390
I want to take care of you now.

1767
02:55:28,340 --> 02:55:30,160
Connie...

1768
02:57:14,190 --> 02:57:15,910
Tom, sit down.

1769
02:57:27,060 --> 02:57:31,260
Our friend and business partner,Hyman Roth, is in the news.

1770
02:57:32,060 --> 02:57:33,850
Did you hear about it?

1771
02:57:34,430 --> 02:57:36,380
I hear that he's in Israel.

1772
02:57:37,400 --> 02:57:38,890
The High Court in Israel

1773
02:57:38,900 --> 02:57:42,120
turned down his request to live there.

1774
02:57:42,130 --> 02:57:45,760
His passport's been invalidated,except to return here.

1775
02:57:45,770 --> 02:57:48,730
He landed in Buenos Aires yesterday.

1776
02:57:48,740 --> 02:57:52,800
He offered them a million dollars if they'd let him live there.

1777
02:57:53,700 --> 02:57:55,900
They turned him down.

1778
02:57:55,910 --> 02:57:57,760
He's going to try Panama.

1779
02:57:57,770 --> 02:57:59,560
Panama won't take him.

1780
02:58:00,030 --> 02:58:02,700
Not for a million, not for ten million

1781
02:58:02,780 --> 02:58:04,300
His condition is reported as terminal.

1782
02:58:04,310 --> 02:58:07,690
He's only got six months left.

1783
02:58:07,700 --> 02:58:10,890
He's had the same heart attack for 20 years.

1784
02:58:10,900 --> 02:58:12,700
That plane goes to Miami.

1785
02:58:12,710 --> 02:58:15,500
That's right. That's where I want it met.

1786
02:58:16,150 --> 02:58:17,870
Impossible.

1787
02:58:17,880 --> 02:58:19,970
They'll turn him over to the Internal Revenue

1788
02:58:19,980 --> 02:58:21,730
Customs and FBI.

1789
02:58:21,740 --> 02:58:23,510
It's not impossible.

1790
02:58:24,050 --> 02:58:25,170
Nothing's impossible.

1791
02:58:26,580 --> 02:58:28,610
There's no way we can get to him!

1792
02:58:28,620 --> 02:58:31,080
Tom, you surprise me.

1793
02:58:33,950 --> 02:58:36,390
If anything in this life is certain...

1794
02:58:37,520 --> 02:58:40,120
...if history has taught us anything...

1795
02:58:40,920 --> 02:58:43,120
...it's that you can kill anyone.

1796
02:58:48,790 --> 02:58:50,350
Rocco?

1797
02:58:50,820 --> 02:58:54,120
Difficult. Not impossible.

1798
02:58:54,130 --> 02:58:56,130
Good.

1799
02:58:58,400 --> 02:59:02,130
Why did you ask me if something was wrong when I came in?

1800
02:59:05,740 --> 02:59:08,160
I thought you were going to tell me

1801
02:59:09,300 --> 02:59:12,000
that you're moving your family to Vegas

1802
02:59:13,040 --> 02:59:17,930
and that you'd been offered the Vice Presidency of the Houstan hotels there.

1803
02:59:18,780 --> 02:59:20,690
- I thought you'd tell me that. -I turned them down.

1804
02:59:20,700 --> 02:59:23,810
Must I tell you every offer I turn down?

1805
02:59:27,950 --> 02:59:30,940
- Let's do business. - All right.

1806
02:59:32,420 --> 02:59:35,380
Just consider this, Michael.Just consider it.

1807
02:59:36,650 --> 02:59:38,970
Roth and the Rosatos are on the run.

1808
02:59:38,980 --> 02:59:41,780
Are they worth it, are we strong enough?

1809
02:59:41,960 --> 02:59:43,840
Is it worth it?

1810
02:59:44,320 --> 02:59:47,010
You've won. Do you want to wipe everybody out?

1811
02:59:47,020 --> 02:59:50,310
I don't feel I have to wipe everybody out, Tom.

1812
02:59:50,520 --> 02:59:53,750
Just my enemies, that's all.

1813
02:59:59,860 --> 03:00:03,450
Are you with me in these things, or what?

1814
03:00:04,560 --> 03:00:05,850
Because if not

1815
03:00:05,860 --> 03:00:08,660
you can take your wife, your family

1816
03:00:08,670 --> 03:00:10,430
and your mistress

1817
03:00:10,530 --> 03:00:12,700
and move them all to Las Vegas.

1818
03:00:16,630 --> 03:00:18,530
Why do you hurt me, Michael?

1819
03:00:18,540 --> 03:00:19,790
I've always been loyal to you.

1820
03:00:19,800 --> 03:00:22,540
What is this?

1821
03:00:26,570 --> 03:00:28,900
So... you're staying?

1822
03:00:29,970 --> 03:00:33,470
-Yes, I'm staying.-Okay.

1823
03:00:35,310 --> 03:00:37,630
What do you want me to do?

1824
03:00:37,670 --> 03:00:39,410
Anthony

1825
03:00:39,880 --> 03:00:41,910
Hey, Anthony...

1826
03:00:41,920 --> 03:00:44,640
How would you like it if I taught you how to catch the really big fish?

1827
03:00:44,650 --> 03:00:47,610
- Would you like that? - Okay.

1828
03:00:47,620 --> 03:00:49,780
You know, when I was your age...

1829
03:00:50,480 --> 03:00:54,140
...I went out fishing with all my brothers

1830
03:00:54,150 --> 03:00:58,140
and my father. Everybody.

1831
03:00:58,650 --> 03:01:01,640
I was the only one that caught a fish.

1832
03:01:01,850 --> 03:01:05,510
Nobody else could catch one.

1833
03:01:05,520 --> 03:01:07,220
Do you know how I did it?

1834
03:01:08,890 --> 03:01:10,680
Every time I put the line in the water

1835
03:01:10,690 --> 03:01:12,480
I said a Hail Mary

1836
03:01:12,690 --> 03:01:15,460
and every time I said a Hail Mary, I caught a fish.

1837
03:01:18,830 --> 03:01:20,320
Do you believe that?

1838
03:01:20,330 --> 03:01:23,190
It's true. That's the secret.

1839
03:01:25,030 --> 03:01:26,890
Do you want to try it out on the lake?

1840
03:01:26,900 --> 03:01:29,570
- Okay.- Okay.

1841
03:01:29,630 --> 03:01:31,100
What else have you got?

1842
03:01:58,890 --> 03:02:01,040
Everything will be okay.

1843
03:02:01,150 --> 03:02:02,580
Did my brother go back?

1844
03:02:02,590 --> 03:02:05,010
Yeah, don't worry.

1845
03:02:05,210 --> 03:02:08,210
He's ten times tougher than me, my brother.

1846
03:02:08,320 --> 03:02:10,420
He's old-fashioned.

1847
03:02:11,460 --> 03:02:12,920
He didn't want dinner

1848
03:02:12,930 --> 03:02:14,680
just wanted to go home.

1849
03:02:14,690 --> 03:02:15,980
That's my brother!

1850
03:02:15,990 --> 03:02:19,850
Nothing could get him away from that two-mule town.

1851
03:02:19,860 --> 03:02:23,280
He could have been big here. He could have had his own family.

1852
03:02:29,100 --> 03:02:33,830
Tom,what do I do now?

1853
03:02:34,970 --> 03:02:36,630
Frankie

1854
03:02:41,500 --> 03:02:45,330
You were always interested in politics and history.

1855
03:02:47,170 --> 03:02:50,190
I remember you talking about Hitler back in '33.

1856
03:02:50,570 --> 03:02:54,360
Yeah, I still read a lot. I get good stuff in there.

1857
03:02:56,850 --> 03:02:59,500
You were around the old-timers

1858
03:02:59,510 --> 03:03:02,460
who built the organisation of the families

1859
